{"id": 58, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "PPRROOJJEECCTT TTAALLKKIINNGG AABBOOUUTT SSPPOORRTTSS MAKE AN INFOGRAPHIC: A CLASS SURVEY REPORT. 11 Look at the infographic from a school magazine on page 111 and check (✓) the correct answers. 1 Who is the infographic for? 33 What questions do you ask? Write the students at school the school soccer team questions in your notebook. 2 What is the infographic about? 1 play soccer? favorite sports the sports students do Can you play soccer? 22 Read the infographic and circle the correct 2 run fast? answers. 1 There are … boys in Class 7A. 3 dance well? a 34 b 12 c 22 2 … girls can dance. 4 play basketball? a 9 b12 c13 3 … boys can play basketball. 5 swim very fast? a 6 b 12 c 15 4 … girls can swim very fast. a 6 b 8 c 12 THINK! 1 Do you do sports with your family? Who? 2 Why are sports good for you? PROJECT TASK 21 PLAN 22 YOUR DIGITAL PORTFOLIO Find out what sports people do in your class. Do a Upload your infographic to the class portfolio for survey, and then create an infographic to show your everyone to see! Present your infographic to the results. class. 1 Choose the sports for your questions. 23 REFLECT 2 Write your questions about sports. Use the questions in Exercise 3, or make new questions. Which is your favorite infographic? Why? 3 Do the survey with your friends in class. 4 Design your infographic. Include two or three ways to show the information. 5 Check grammar, spelling, and punctuation. 110 PROJECT TALKING ABOUT SPORTS Class 7A Survey about sports 22 PLAY SOCCER 34 There are 12 girls and STUDENTS 22 boys in 7 girls Class 7A. and 15 boys can play soccer. 5 girls and 7 boys can’t play soccer. 16 run 21 dance 6 girls and 10 boys 12 girls can run fast. and 9 boys can dance. 6 girls and 12 boys can’t run fast. 13 boys boys can’t 20 dance. PLAY BASKETBALL 34 swim 8 girls and 12 boys 22 boys can play basketball. 12 girls 12 boys 4 girls 6 girls and 10 boys can’t play basketball. …can swim …can swim very fast Don’t forget to do exercise for 6 0 minutes a day! It’s good for you! PROJECTS 111", "page": 114, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 59, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "B R E V LIST Verb Unit Page Verb Unit Page Verb Unit Page ask 5 58 hang out 5 60 run 8 88 be 1 14 happen 6 73 see 6 72 become 6 68 hate 6 69 sell 6 69 bring 7 84 have 4 46 send 7 84 buy 7 80 help 6 68 show 7 84 catch 8 89 hope 5 58 sit 7 84 chat 5 58 ice-skate 8 88 ski 8 88 close 7 80 improve 8 94 speak 2 28 come 6 68 increase 8 94 spell 0 10 communicate 2 28 kick 8 89 spend 5 63 compete 8 94 know 5 62 start 5 58 cost 6 68 learn 6 71 stay 6 69 create 8 95 like 5 58 study 5 58 dance 8 88 listen 0 10 surf 8 88 develop 8 94 live 5 60 swim 8 88 do 5 56 look 0 10 take 5 56 dress 7 84 love 4 50 talk 2 24 drink 8 92 mean 0 10 teach 6 68 eat 6 74 meet 0 6 text 6 68 exist 2 26 mind 5 62 think 6 72 feel 8 94 order 6 68 throw 8 89 finish 5 58 play 5 56 travel 5 62 fly 5 63 post 2 24 use 2 27 forget 6 68 practice 5 62 walk 8 89 get 7 80 protect 7 84 watch 5 58 get up 5 56 put on 8 93 wear 7 79 go 5 56 read 0 10 work 5 58 go out 5 64 reduce 8 94 write 0 10 guess 2 24 represent 6 73 112", "page": 115, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 60, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "MAR M GRA REFERENCE BE Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Questions (?) Short Answers I am (’m) Spanish I am (’m) not Spanish. Am I Spanish? Yes, I am. No, I’m not. You / We / They are (’re) You / We / They are not Are you / we / they Yes, you / we / they are. Spanish. (aren’t) Spanish. Spanish? No, you / we / they aren’t. He / She / It is (’s) He / She / It is not (isn’t) Is he / she / it Spanish? Yes, he / she / it is. Spanish. Spanish. No, he / she / it isn’t. Where ... from? Where am I from? I’m from Spain. I’m not from Spain. Where are you from? You’re from Azerbaijan. You’re not from Azerbaijan. Where are they from? They’re from England. They’re not from England. Where’s he/she/it from? He’s/She’s/It’s from He’s/She’s/It’s not from South Africa. South Africa. HAVE Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Questions (?) Short Answers I / You / We / They (’ve) I / You / We / They do Do I / you / we / they Yes, I / you / we / they have a phone. not (don’t) have a have a phone? do. phone. No, I / you / we / they don’t. He / She / It has (‘s) a He / She / It does not Does he / she / it have a Yes, he / she / it does. phone. (doesn’t) have a phone. phone? No, he / she / it doesn’t. 113", "page": 116, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 61, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "GRAMMAR REFERENCE PRESENT SIMPLE Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Questions (?) Short Answers I / You / We / They live I / You / We / They do Do I / you / we / they Yes, I / you / we / they do. in Madrid. not (don’t) live in Madrid. live in Madrid? No, I / you / we / they don’t. He / She / It lives in He / She / It does not Does he / she / it live in Yes, he / she / it does. Madrid. (doesn’t) live in Madrid. Madrid? No, he / she / it doesn’t. CAN: ABILITY Affirmative (+) Negative (-) I can play football. I can’t play baseball. He/She/It can run five kilometers. He/She/It can’t run five kilometers. We can make pizza. We can’t make pizza. You can speak French. You can’t speak French. They can dance. They can’t dance. Yes/No Questions Short Answers Can I walk? Yes, I can./No, I can’t. Can you play basketball? Yes, you can./No, you can’t. Can he/she/it catch the ball? Yes, he/she/it can. / No, he/she/it can’t. Can they swim? Yes, they can./No, they can’t. THERE IS / THERE ARE Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Questions (?) Short Answers There is (’s) a desk in There is not (isn’t) a Is there a desk in the Yes, there is. the bedroom. desk in the bedroom. bedroom? No, there isn’t. There are (‘re) some There are not (aren’t) Are there any apples? Yes, there are. apples. any apples. No, there aren’t. 114 PRESENT CONTINUOUS Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Questions (?) Short Answers I am (’m) eating. I am (’m) not eating. Am I eating? Yes, I am. No, I’m not. You / We / They are (’re) You / We / They are not Are you / we / they Yes, you / we / they are. eating. (aren’t) eating. eating? No, you / we / they aren’t. He / She / It is (’s) He / She / It is not (isn’t) Is he / she / it eating? Yes, he / she / it is. eating. eating. No, he / she / it isn’t. IMPERATIVES Affirmative (+) Negative (–) Stand up! Open the book! Don’t stand up! Don’t open the book! QUESTION WORDS What What is your favorite color? Where Where are you from? How How do you make a paper plane? Who Who is your best friend? How old How old is your dad? When When does our flight leave? 115", "page": 118, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 62, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "GRAMMAR REFERENCE PERSONAL PRONOUNS AND POSSESSIVE ADJECTIVES I am You are an He is a the She is from It is a car. We are They are Spanish. excellent headteacher. Azerbaijan. football chefs in student. fans. a nice restaurant. My Your best His name is Her Its interior is Our Their language is subject is Daniel. nationality is all white. favourite food is Spanish. maths. Azerbaijani. team is spectacular. Liverpool. POSSESSIVE ’S Singular Plural Irregular Beth’s computer his parents’ house the women’s football team the boy’s bike the students’ books the children’s favourite toy 116 Adapted by: content – Ulkar Babayeva, Shahana Mammadli, Habiba Nazirova, Solmaz Jahangirova, design – Eldaniz Khojazada Game Changer Student Book as the main foreign language Azerbaijan edition Language for the 5th grade of the general education schools Account-publishing volume: 16.5. Physical print sheet: 15. Number of pages: 120. After cropping: 210 × 297. Font and size: Helvetica, Avenir, Laca, Abolition, Brink, DIN2014, American Captain, 10pt. Offset printing. Order 0394. Circulation:148 050. Free. Baku - 2024 The date of the collection and signature of the manuscript: 02.07.2024 Adapter of the printed product: Educational Institute of the Republic of Azerbaijan (Baku city, A. Jalilov street, 96). First published 2024 ISBN 978-1-009-79635-4 Game Changer Student Book as the main foreign language Azerbaijan edition Cambridge 117 dizayn − Eldəniz Xocazadə Game Changer dərslik 5 Azərbaycan nəşri Ümumi təhsil müəssisələrinin 5-ci sinifləri üçün İngilis dili (əsas xarici dil) fənni üzrə dərslik. Hesab-nəşriyyat həcmi: 16,5. Fiziki çap vərəqi: 15. Səhifə sayı: 120. Kəsimdən sonra: 210 × 297. Şrift və ölçü: Helvetica, Avenir, Laca, Abolition, Brink, DIN2014, American Captain, 10pt. Ofset çapı. Sifariş 0394. Tiraj: 148 050. Pulsuz. Bakı – 2024 Əlyazmanın yığıma verildiyi və çapa imzalandığı tarix: 02.07.2024 Çap məhsulunu uyğunlaşdıran: Azərbaycan Respublikasının Təhsil İnstitutu (Bakı ş., A.Cəlilov küç., 96). Çap məhsulunu istehsal edən: “Şərq-Qərb” ASC (Bakı ş., Aşıq Ələsgər küç., 17) İlk nəşr 2024 ISBN 978-1-009-79635-4 Game Changer Student Book as the main foreign language Azerbaijan edition Cambridge University 118", "page": 121, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
