{"id": 5, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 1 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples below and complete the sentences from the poster. Verb to be Affirmative (+) Long Form Short Form I am Olivia. I’ m Olivia. You are my friend. You’re my friend. He/She is two, and he/she is very happy! He’s/She’ two, and he’s/she’s very happy! It is cool! It’ cool! We are awesome! We’ awesome! They are cool! They’re cool! 2 Change the underlined parts of the sentences. Use the example to help you. 1 The teachers are great! They’re great! 2 Flamenco is a type of music and dance. 3 My friend and I are happy. 4 Evelyn is my favorite friend. 5 Kamran is a cool student. 3 Choose the correct words. LOOK! 1 Aynur is / are my teacher. 5 I ’m / ’re a student. 2 Max am / is my dog. 6 We’ s / ’re friends! Max is my dog. He’s my dog. 3 My jeans is / are blue. 7 You is / are happy. 4 My bike is / are at home. 4 Complete the text with the correct forms of the verb to be. My name’s Maria and I 1 ’m 12 years old. I 2 in 5th grade at Meridian Forest School. My favorite thing 3 my cell phone. My favorite friends 4 Lucia and Marco. They 5 cool! 15 WORKBOOK p.2, p.5 and p.6 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 Look at the image. Audrey is … in the classroom. at the yoga club. 2 1.03 Listen to the dialogue and check your answer. 3 1.04 Listen to the fi rst part of the dialogue again and check (✓) the correct answers. 1 The dialogue is about ... registration at a new club. registration at a new school. 2 Yoga classes are ... on Friday. on Wednesday. 4 1.03 Listen to the dialogue again and complete the information about Audrey. YYYYYYYOOOOOOOGGGGGGGAAAAAAA CCCCCCCLLLLLLLUUUUUUUBBBBBBB RRRRRRREEEEEEEGGGGGGGIIIIIIISSSSSSSTTTTTTTRRRRRRRAAAAAAATTTTTTTIIIIIIIOOOOOOONNNNNNN FFFFFFFOOOOOOORRRRRRRMMMMMMM Activity: First Name: AAuuddrreeyy Last Name: Age: Grade: Address: LLiiggeerr SSttrreeeett Home Phone Number:555- 5 1.05 Match 1–7 with a–g. Then listen, check, and repeat. 1 Jones a grade 2 15 Park Road b name of school 3 13 c phone number 4 Green Tree School d address 5 7th e fi rst name 6 555-5281 f age 7 James g last name 16 WORKBOOK p.2 and p.3", "page": 19, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 6, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 1 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the questions from the dialogue with the words below. Answer the questions in the chart that are true for you. • What • How • Who • How old Wh- questions Wh- Questions Answers Me What ’s your phone number? It’s 555-5436. is your teacher? Mr. Avery. are you today? I’m good, thanks. are you? I’m 12 years old. 2 Complete the chart. Use the correct forms of the verb to be. Verb to be Negative (-) Long Form Short Form I amnot Olivia. I’m not Olivia. You are not my favorite friend. You’re not (aren’t) my favorite friend. He/She is not very happy! He’s/She’s not very happy. It not cool! It’s not (isn’t) cool! We are not awesome! not awesome! They are not cool! cool! 3 Correct the sentences so they are true for you. Use the example to help you. 1 I’m in 8th grade. I’m not in 8th grade. I’m in 6th grade. 2 I’m nine years old. 3 My teacher is Ms. Malahat. 4 My phone number is 555-5550. 5 My friends are Samir and Parvana. USE IT! 4 Ask your partner questions with the words below and complete the chart with his/her answers. Name Last Name Address Teacher Age Phone Number WORKBOOK p.2, p.4 and p.7 17 AARROOUUNNDD TTHHEE WWOORRLLDD www.globalteenstudents.net HHHOOOMMMEEE WWWHHHOOO WWWEEE AAARRREEE BBBBLLLLOOOOGGGG JJJJOOOOIIIINNNN SSuunnddaayy,, MMaayy 2211 ((uuppddaatteedd eevveerryy ddaayy)) GGLLOOBBAALL TTEEEENN SSttuuddeennttss ffrroomm ddiiffff eerreenntt ccuullttuurreess aarroouunndd tthhee wwoorrlldd SSTTUUDDEENNTTSS aarree oonn oouurr wweebb ppaaggee.. LLeett’’ss mmeeeett tthhrreeee BByy SSttuuddeennttss ffoorr SSttuuddeennttss,, ooff tthheemm ttooddaayy!! WWee AArree tthhee WWoorrlldd.. LLeett’’ss MMaakkee FFrriieennddss!! LLUUKKAA,, CCRROOAATTIIAA HHii,, II’’mm LLuukkaa.. II’’mm 1133 yyeeaarrss oolldd aanndd II’’mm aa ssttuuddeenntt.. ThTh iiss iiss mmyy ccaammeerraa,, aanndd tthhiiss iiss mmyy iiddeennttiittyy:: mmyy bbeeaauuttiiffuull ccoouunnttrryy aanndd mmyy pphhoottooss ooff iitt.. CCoommmmeennttss:: POST CAMILA, HONDURAS Hey, I’m Camila, and I’m 12. For me, family is very important. When I’m with my family, life is fun! My friends are important too, but my family is fi rst. Comments: POST KABALI, NAMIBIA Hello! My name’s Kabali. I’m 11 and I like music. But music is not my favorite thing. Nature is! Nature is very important to me and my community. Comments: POST 18", "page": 21, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 7, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 1 1 Look at the web page. Complete the website address. www. 2 1.06 Read and listen to the web page and check (✓) the correct answers. 1 What’s it about? world problems students of the world 2 Who’s on the web page? students students and teachers 3 How old is Kabali? 11 12 3 Read the web page again. Check (✓) what’s important for the students. Luka Camila Kabali nature family and friends photography WORDS IN CONTEXT 4 Find the words on the web page and then explain them to your partner. Use a dictionary to help you. 1 beautiful 2 country 3 photo 4 fun THINK! Find three photos of your country that are important for you. Why are they important? VIDEO 1.2 1 What is Kasia’s favorite activity? 2 What is Trevor’s favorite activity? 1199 SPEAKING GIVING PERSONAL INFORMATION 1 Look at the image. The dialogue is about … 4 1.08 Listen and repeat the expressions. dance. music. PRONUNCIATION /uː/ 2 1.07 Read and listen to Ellis and Audrey. 5 1.09 Listen and repeat. Ellis Hi, I’m Ellis. What’s your name? Audrey I’m Audrey. Ellis How old are you? Me too! Audrey I’m 12. Yes, it’s cool. Ellis Me too. Audrey You’re great! Ellis Oh, really? Thanks! Ballet is my 6 1.07 Listen to the dialogue again. Then favorite activity. practice with a partner. Audrey Yes, it’s cool. 7 Role play a new dialogue. Follow the steps. Ellis Let’s text! What’s your phone number? 1 Change the words in blue to write a new Audrey It’s 555-5436. dialogue in your notebook. Ellis Thanks! 2 Practice your dialogue with a partner. 3 Present your dialogue to the class. LIVING ENGLISH 3 Complete the mini dialogues with the expressions below. • You’re great! • Me too. • Let’s text. 1 A How old are you? B I’m 11. A 2 A What’s your phone number? B It’s 555-9867. A OK, 3 A Ballet is my favorite activity. B A Oh, really? Thanks! 20 2 ENGLISH UNIT GOALS EVERYWHERE! • Talk about countries, nationalities, and languages. • Read a forum. • Listen to a radio show. • Learn about English around the world. • Write a post on an online forum. VIDEO 2.1 THINK! VIDEO 1 Say two reasons why people 5.1 need English to communicate. 1 Where is English around you? Name the countries in the video. 2 WAhriceh d caoiluy nrotruietisn deso syiomui lsaer ea rino und 2 Why is it important to learn English? thteh evi dweoor?ld? 21", "page": 24, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 8, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 2.01 Look at the web page and complete the nationalities with the words below. Then listen, check, and repeat. • American • Brazilian • British • French • Japanese • Mexican • Russian • South African • Spanish www.penpalsworld.net/penpals/NATIONALITIES WWWWeeeellllccccoooommmmeeee ttttoooo PPPPeeeennnn PPPPaaaallllssss WWWWoooorrrrlllldddd!!!! MMaakkee ffrriieennddss aarroouunndd tthhee wwoorrlldd!! 2 3 1 Adrien Age: 12 Ana Maria Nationality: Age: 13 Age: 11 From: Paris, France Nationality: 4 Nationality: American Favorite things: music, clothes From: Madrid, Spain From: Los Angeles, the United States Favorite things: j eans, bike SSaayy HHii Favorite things: Internet, cell phone SSaayy HHii RRUUSSSSIIAA Say HHii UUKK Alisa FFRRAANNCCEE Age: 13 UUSSAA JJAAPPAANN Nationality: SSPPAAIINN From: Moscow, Russia 5 MMEEXXIICCOO Favorite things: soccer, food SSaayy HHii 9 BBRRAAZZIILL Alejandro SSOOUUTTHH Age: 12 AAFFRRIICCAA Nationality: From: M exico City, Mexico Tomomi Favorite things: soccer, music Age: 13 Say HHii 7 8 Nationality: From: Osaka, Japan 6 Favorite things: sports, clothes Say HHii Jack Kungawo Age: 14 Age: 11 Adriana Nationality: Nationality: Age: 12 From: London, the United Kingdom From: Cape Town, South Africa Nationality: Favorite things: sports, friends Favorite things: Internet, music From: R ecife, Brazil Favorite things: food, friends Say HHii Say HHii Say HHii 22 UNIT 2 2 2.02 Complete the chart with the countries or nationalities. Use the web page to help you. Then listen, check, and repeat. Flag Country Nationality 1 Brazil Brazilian 2 The United States r c n 3 South Africa South n 4 a Japanese 5 R a n 6 Spain S h 7 M LOOK! Use CAPITAL LETTERS with countries and nationalities. 8 The United Kingdom B h I’m from the United States. I’m American. 9 F I’m from Mexico. I’m Mexican. 3 L ook at the web page again. Where are they from? Complete the sentences. 1 Adrien is from France . He’s French . 2 Ana is from . She’s . 3 Kungawo is from . He’s . 4 Tomomi is from . She’s . 5 Jack is from . He’s . 6 Alisa is from . She’s . WORKBOOK p.9 23", "page": 26, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 9, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING www.penpalsworld.net Forums >> General >> People Masonboy10 Posted at 10:32 Hey guys! How about a game? Post TWO images and people guess your nationality or your country. Th ese are my two pictures. What’s my nationality? REPLY UnicornsAreAwesome Posted at 10:35 Masonboy10. Are you from the United Kingdom? Hmm. Oh, no! You’re from the United States. You’re American! What about me? Where am I from? English is the offi cial language in my country. REPLY McCupcake Posted at 10:42 Beautiful! Is it the Maracanã Stadium? Are you from Rio de Janeiro? Wait, no, you’re not. English is not the offi cial language of Brazil!! Are you South African? Oh, yes, you are. Th at’s the Cape Town Stadium! Now guess MY nationality. REPLY Monte@home Posted at 11:15 Wait! Is it Mexico? Oh, yes, it is! I’m Mexican, too! Look! Where’s Mariana, my pen pal, from? REPLY UnicornsAreAwesome Posted at 11:18 Th at’s Copacabana beach. Is she from Brazil? REPLY Monte@home Posted at 11:22 Yes, she is! Good job! REPLY 1 Look at the text, images, and design. What is it? Check (✓) the correct answer. a magazine article a forum 2 What is the objective of this type of text? Check (✓) the correct answer. to express an opinion to talk to different people 3 2.03 Read and listen to the text. Decide if the sentences are T (true) or F (false). 1 Masonboy10 is from the United Kingdom. F 2 UnicornsAreAwesome is from South Africa. 3 McCupcake is from Brazil. 4 Two people are Mexican. 5 Monte@home is from Spain. THINK! What two pictures represent your nationality? Why? 24 UNIT 2 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples below. Complete the sentences from the forum. Verb to be Yes/No questions Short Answers Am I right? Yes, I am. No, I’m not. Are you from Rio de Janeiro? , you are. No, you . Is he/she/it from South Africa? , he/she/it is. , he’s/she’s/it’s not (isn’t). Are we Mexican? , we are. , we’re not (aren’t). Are they from Brazil? , they are. , they’re not (aren’t). Where … from? I Where am I from? I’m from the United Kingdom. I’m not from the United Kingdom. you Where are you from? You’re from Brazil. You’re not from Brazil. they Where are they from? They’re from Mexico. They’re not from Mexico. he/she/it Where’s he/she/it from? He’s/She's/It's from Japan. He’s/She's/It's not from Japan. 2 Ask questions. Use the words in parentheses. 1 (you / Russia?) 4 (your classmates / India) Are you from Russia? No, I'm not. I'm from South Africa. (your teacher / the United (your friend / Brazil) 2 5 Kingdom?) 3 (your cell phone / Japan) USE IT! What’s your name? My name’s …. 3 Your partner is a famous person. Are you Spanish? No, I’m not. I’m … Interview him/her. WORKBOOK p.8, p.11 and p.12 25", "page": 28, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 10, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 2.04 Look at the pictures. What are their names in English? Listen, check, and repeat. 1 2 3 4 ketchup 5 6 7 8 2 2.05 Listen to the radio show. Number the words in the order you hear them from 1–8. chocolate hamburger hotel jeans ketchup 1 pizza restaurant taxi 3 What is the radio show about? Check (✓) the correct answer. English in Brazil favorite words 4 2.05 Listen to the radio show again. Decide if the sentences are T (true) or F (false). 1 Caio and Gabriela are on a radio show. T 2 Caio is from Brazil. 3 Jeans is a Spanish word. 4 There are English words and expressions in Brazilian Portuguese. 5 The word chocolate exists in many different languages. USE IT! 5 What are your favorite English words? Make a list. Then compare with a partner. 26 WORKBOOK p.8 and p.9 UNIT 2 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Choose the correct answer according to the information in the radio show. Possessive (’s) Caio and Gabriela’s topic is English in Brazil / on the radio. Caio’s fi rst language is English / Portuguese. Children’s favorite word is chocolate / pizza. 2 Complete the phrases. John Ali and Ayan Lisa The people 2 3 4 1 John’s notebook dog cell phone favorite band 3 Complete the sentences in the chart with the words below. • Its • His • Their Personal Pronouns Possessive Adjectives I’m Azerbaijani. My fi rst language is Azerbaijani. LOOK! You’re a good student. Your English is good. Use their for He’s a radio show host. name is Caio. boys and girls. Sergio and She’s from Japan. Her nationality is Japanese. Katia’s bikes. It’s a pizza restaurant. name is Dino’s Pizza. Their bikes. We’re soccer fans. Our favorite team is Barça. They’re American. country is the United States. 4 Choose the correct possessive adjectives. 1 Gabriela is on the radio. I like her / my radio show. 4 This is my school. Our / Its name is Park School. 2 This is my friend. His / Its name is Marco. 5 This is Jane’s bike and this is Max’s bike. 3 We’re from Mexico. Her / Our nationality is Mexican. Their / His bikes are blue. USE IT! 5 Copy the chart to your notebook. Complete the questions and answer them for you. Then interview your partner. Questions Me My Partner What’s name? What’s favorite color? Who’s friend? What’s phone number? 6 Make four sentences about your partner. WORKBOOK p.8, p.10 and p.13 27", "page": 30, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 11, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "AACCRROOSSSS TTHHEE CCUURRRRIICCUULLUUMM GEOGRAPHY English is Everywhere! HI! HELLO! Are you an English HEY! student? Good for you! Look at these facts about the English language: 1/5 English is a global language. About 1.5 billion people in the world are English speakers. That’s 20% of the world population! 380 But only 380 million people in the world are “native” English speakers. million They’re from countries where English is the fi rst language or native language: Australia, the United Kingdom, the United States, and others. English is the language of science, commerce, sports, and tourism! I’m your Are you a tourist? Are you pilot. on a plane? English is the English words are in offi cial language for pilots. diff erent languages in many Your pilot is an English countries. speaker! In Mexico, many English words are very popular such as casual, spoiler 8800%% and hashtag! English words are common in Japan, too! Technology, computers, and (suu-paa): supermarket スーパー social media are places for (ho-te-ru) hotel English, too! Over 80% of the ホテル words on computers are in (re-su-to-ran): restaurant レストラン English. So, be part of this community! Speak English and communicate with the world! 28 UUNNIITT 22 1 Look at the infographic on page 28. Choose the correct words to make a true sentence. This infographic is a visual / long text with opinions / facts. 2 What’s the infographic’s central idea? Check (✓) the correct answer. English as an official language the number of English speakers in the world the importance of English around the world English words in Japanese 3 Scan the infographic and match the numbers (1–4) with the facts (a–d). 1 7.5 a number of English native speakers in the world 2 380,000,000 b number of English speakers in the world 3 4/5 c world population, in billions 4 1,500,000,000 d proportion of English words on computers in the world 4 Read the infographic. Complete the information. 1 Two countries where English words are common, but people don’t speak English as a first language: Mexico and Japan . 2 Three countries where English is the native language: , , and . 3 English is important in these activities: , , and . 4 English is the official language for this profession: . WORDS IN CONTEXT 5 Complete the sentences with the expressions below. • native speakers • social media • global language • native language • official language 1 Japanese English students are not native speakers of English. 2 English is the of the FIFA World Cup. 3 English is a . People speak it all over the world. 4 Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram are all examples of 5 Portuguese is the of Brazilians. THINK! VIDEO Why is English important to you? 2.2 1 How many singers in the video sing in English? 2 Say the countries you hear in the video. 2299", "page": 32, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 12, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "W WRRIITTIINNGG 11 2.06 Read and listen to the post from a forum. What’s the topic? Check (✓) the correct answer. an online game a popular movie English words www.penpalsworld.net Forums >> General >> Languages | English Words Every Day LavenderLiz Posted at 4 p.m. Hello, everyone! I’m Brazilian, from Porto Alegre. Portuguese is our offi cial language in Brazil, but English words are very popular. Th ey’re everywhere: restaurant names, foods, places, computers, etc. Here’s my list: download, Wi-Fi, playlist, videogame, and notebook. My favorite word is playlist, because music is fun! How about you? Where are you from? What are your everyday English words? What’s your favorite? Write a comment about it. COMMENT SHARE c LIKE ♥ 22 Read the post again. Who is the post for? Choose the correct answer. People in the forum / Italy / your country. 33 Read the post again and answer the questions. 1 Which phrase is a greeting? Hello, everyone! 2 Find words for nationality, origin, and language. LOOK! 3 Which phrase introduces a list of English words? How about you? = And you? 4 Find four questions for the reader. 44 Write a reply to the post in your notebook. 1 Take notes: Write the name of your favorite country, your city and your language. Make a list of common everyday English words for you. Then underline your favorite word. 2 Write your comment. Use the elements in 1. 55 Change your comment with a partner and check his/her work. Use the checklist below. Name of the country? List of English words? Favorite word? 30", "page": 33, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 13, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "REVIEW UNITS 1 AND 2 VOCABULARY 1 Find the odd one out. 1 sports / music / pizza 3 school uniform / taxi / jeans 2 chocolate / hamburger / clothes 4 school / bike / cell phone 2 Complete the interview with information about you. 1 What’s your last name? 3 What’s your address? 2 How old are you? 4 What’s your phone number? 3 Put the letters in the correct order to complete the sentences. Where are the people from? 1 She’s from ABREZJNAIA AZERBAIJAN . 3 He’s from RALIBZ . 2 She’s from PNAJA . 4 She’s from APNIS . 4 Complete the sentences with the correct nationality. 1 I’m from Azerbaijan. I’m Azerbaijani . 2 She’s from Russia. She’s . 3 We’re from the United Kingdom. We’re . 4 He’s from South Africa. He’s . 5 Match the questions (1–5) with the answers (a–e). 1 Are you happy? a No, he’s not. 2 Is he cool? b They’re my friends. 3 Who are they? c I’m 12. 4 How old are you? d No, she’s not. 5 Is she your teacher? e No, I’m not. 6 Read the text. Then ask and answer the questions. Hi, I’m Alicia Patel, and I’m 12. I’m from Spain. I’m a student at the International School, and I’m in grade 7. Joshua and Nina are my friends. We’re in the same class. Joshua is from the United Kingdom, and Nina is from the United States. We’re international students. 1 Alicia / Spain? Is Alicia from Spain? Yes, she is. 2 Alicia / teacher? 3 Alicia / sixth grade? 4 Joshua / the United Kingdom? 31 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 7 Look at the pictures and make sentences. 1 Fidan / bike / blue 3 Isaac / cell phone / black Fidan bike is blue. 2 Hugo / English / dictionary / new 4 Felipe and Kathy / favorite / food / pizza 8 Complete the sentences with the words in the box. • her • his • my • our 1 Anna is my friend. Her last name is Green. 3 He’s a student. name is Chingiz. 2 We’re Japanese. country is Japan. 4 I am Brazilian. Brazil is country. Check your progress I CAN... • talk about favorite things. • use the verb to be to give personal information. • talk about countries and nationalities. • use possessive adjectives and ’s. Learn to learn Dictionary Entry entry/word grammar function bike pronunciation noun [ informal ] meaning UK /baɪk/ US /baɪk/ short form of “bicycle”: Source: https://dictionary.cambridge.org/ dictionary/english-portuguese/bike 32", "page": 35, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 14, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "3 WHERE'S UNIT GOALS • Talk about different parts E? O M of a house and furniture. H • Read about a house. • Listen to a video chat. • Learn about houses around the world. • Talk about your house and furniture. VIDEO THINK! 3.1 1 Say what types of homes are in these places: 1 Imagine you live in this house. towns 5 a .1 nd cities, the countryside, on water. What are your favorite things about it? 2 What three things does the video say are 2 Why is home important? important in a home? 33 VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 3.01 Complete Katia’s messages with the words below. Then listen, check, and repeat. • bathroom • bedroom • dining room • kitchen • living room • yard Places at Home 1 This is my bedroom . 4 This is the . It’s small, but nice. It’s really nice! 2 5 Here’s the . Here’s the – It’s really modern! and Julia’s cat! 3 6 The is Look at the – and awesome. It’s very big! the bikes. They’re very old! LOOK! really + adjective It’s really nice! very + adjective It’s very old. 34 UNIT 3 2 3.02 Where are the things? Write the places with the words in Exercise 1 in your notebook. Then listen, check, and repeat. 1 In the bedroom . 1 2 3 2 In the . 3 In the . 4 In the . 4 5 6 5 In the . 6 In the . 3 3.03 Look at the images and choose the correct words. Then listen, check, and repeat. 1 2 3 A small / big house A small / modern apartment A(n) old / modern kitchen 4 5 A(n) old / nice bathroom A nice / big bedroom 4 Copy the chart to your notebook and complete it with words from Exercises 2 and 3. thbedroom us the bus the bus the bus the bus Adjectives the bus Parts of the bus the House the bus the bus the bus the bus WORKBOOK p.15 35", "page": 38, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 15, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 1 Look at the text and the image, and answer the questions. Check (✓) the correct answers. 1 What type of text is this? a blog a dialogue from a chat app 2 What is the topic of the conversation? a trip a house Hi, I’m Jakob. I’m from Norway. I’m 11. This is my home. It’s diff erent! It’s a stilt1 house. There’s one bathroom, and it’s small! There are three small bedrooms. My favorite place is my bedroom. It’s not big, but it’s awesome. There’s a bed, and a table (and my cell phone)! There isn't a yard, but there’s a place for my bike. My bike is my favorite thing! My family’s favorite place is the living room. It’s big and modern. There’s a kitchen and a dining room in one room. It’s small and old, but very nice. My friend, Filip, is in the dining room. Today, there aren’t any hamburgers, but there is pizza. Yummy! Where are you from? Is your home diff erent? 1 A house placed on long pieces of wood or metal 2 3.04 Read and listen to the text. Complete the chart about Jakob’s home with the correct number of rooms. Jakob’s Home kitchen/dining room 1 bathroom yard living room bedroom 3 Read the text again and answer the questions. 1 Where is Jakob from? 4 What is Jakob’s favorite thing? Jakob is from Norway. 2 How old is he? 5 What is his family’s favorite place? 3 What is Jakob’s favorite place? 6 Who is Filip? THINK! What’s your favorite place in your house? Why? 36 UNIT 3 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples below and complete the sentences from Jakob’s blog. There is/There are LOOK! Affi rmative (+) Negative (-) Use any for plural nouns: There’s a kitchen. There a yard. There aren’t any cars. There three There any small bedrooms. hamburgers. 2 Choose the correct words. My house is nice. 1There’s / There’re two bedrooms and 2there’s / there’re two bathrooms for my family. 3There’s / There’re a living room, but 4there isn’t / there aren’t a dining room. 5There isn’t / There aren’t a yard. My bike is in my bedroom! My favorite place is the kitchen, but 6there isn’t / there aren’t any pizza today! 3 Look at the house and complete the sentences with there’s, there isn’t, there’re, and there aren’t. 1 There’s a living room. 2 two bedrooms. 3 any people in the house. 4 a dining room. 5 a bathroom. 6 two kitchens. USE IT! Tell me about your house. 4 Work in pairs. Give information about your house. There are two bedrooms. There isn’t a yard. WORKBOOK p.14, p.17 and p.18 37", "page": 40, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 16, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 3.05 Match the images with the words below. Then listen, check, and repeat. • bed • chair • closet • door • shower • table • wall • window 1 2 3 4 bed 5 6 7 8 2 3.06 Katia and Maria are on a video call. Listen and check (✓) the correct bedroom. 1 2 3 3.06 Listen to the video call again. Choose the correct answers. 1 Where is Katia? 4 Where are Katia’s clothes? a in her bedroom b in Julia’s bedroom a in Julia’s bedroom b in her bedroom 2 What color is Katia’s chair? 5 Who is at the door? a blue b green a Maria b Julia 3 Where are Katia’s jeans? a on her table b on her bed LOOK! TThhee ppiiccttuurree iiss oonn tthhee wwaallll.. TThhee bbooookkss aarree oonn tthhee ttaabbllee.. TThhee cchhaaiirr iiss iinn tthhee lliivviinngg rroooomm.. 38 WORKBOOK p.14 and p.15 UNIT 3 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the questions and answers from the video call in the chart with the words below. • Is • there is • No • Are there • are There is/There are Yes/No questions Short Answers Is there a picture on the wall? Yes, . Is there a closet? , there isn’t. any books? Yes, there . Are there any cats in the bedroom? No, there aren’t. 2 Put the words in the correct order to make questions. 1 bed / there / a / kitchen / Is / in / the / ? Is there a bed in the kitchen? 4 Are / living /chairs / in / room / the / there / two / ? 2 your / books / in / Are / bedroom / there / any / ? 5 bedroom / closet / there / a / Is / the / in / ? 3 kitchen / a / Is / there / the / table / in / ? 3 Look at this room and answer the questions. Give short answers. 1 Is there a closet? Yes, there is. 2 Is there a bed? 3 Are there two chairs? 4 Is there a picture on the wall? 5 Are there any windows? USE IT! 4 Copy the chart to your notebook. Check (✓) the objects in your bedroom. closet chair table pictures on the wall window Me My Partner 5 Work in pairs. Ask and answer questions about your bedrooms. Check (✓) your Is there a closet in your bedroom? Yes, there is. partner’s objects. WORKBOOK p.14, p.16 and p.19 39", "page": 42, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 17, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "AARROOUUNNDD THE WORLD Home Sweet Home HOME ON WATER H ello, my name’s Leo and I’m from England, in the UK. My home is a houseboat on the River Stort. My friends at school are curious1 about it because it’s on the river, and it’s diff erent. My home is not big, but it’s comfortable. There are two bedrooms, a living room, a kitchen, and a bathroom. There aren’t any walls between the living room and the kitchen. There’s a stove, a fridge, and a small table with chairs. There isn’t a sofa, but there are many pictures on the wall and many vases with plants. My parents are fans of nature. • • • There’s a TV, too. Oh, and soccer on TV is • my favorite thing! • • My favorite place at home is my • bedroom. In my bedroom, there’s a bed, • a closet with my comic books and my • clothes, a table, and a chair. Ah, and I’m • a music student, so of course there’s my • guitar, too. • • And you? What’s your home like and • • what’s your favorite place at home? • • Teen World 36 1 Interested in learning about people and things around you 40 UNIT 3 1 Look at the text and the images. Then complete the sentences with the words below. • magazine • section • title 1 This text is from a . WORDS IN CONTEXT 2 The name of the is Home Sweet Home. 3 The of the article is Home on Water. 3 Name the pictures with the words in the box. 2 3.07 Read and listen to the text and complete the notes. • river • comic book • stove • vase 1 Leo’s country: England 2 Leo’s home location: 1 3 Number of rooms in Leo’s home: 4 Object not present in Leo’s home: 5 Leo’s favorite place at home: river 4 Find the words in the text. Explain them to your partner. Use a dictionary to help you. 2 1 comfortable 2 comic 3 curious 4 fan 5 move 5 Complete the sentences with expressions from the text. 3 1 Nature is their favorite thing. They’re . 2 I’m a sports fan. Soccer on TV is my . 6 Match the causes (1–4) with the results (a–d). 4 1 Leo’s house is different. 2 Soccer on TV is Leo’s favorite thing. 3 Leo’s parents are fans of nature. 4 Leo’s a music student. a There’s a TV in the house. b There’s a guitar in his room. c His friends are curious. d There are many vases with plants inside. THINK! VIDEO Are you curious about your friends’ homes? 3.2 Are they curious about your home? Why? 1 What countries do you hear in the video? 2 What’s your favorite home? 4411", "page": 44, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 18, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "SPEAKING REACTING POSITIVELY 21 3.08 Read and listen to Henry and Layla. Where’s Henry? Henry Hey, Layla! Look at my dining room! Isn’t it great? Layla Oh, wow! What’s that? Is it a table? Henry Yes, it is. It’s a Japanese table. Now look at theliving room. Layla What? There aren’t any chairs! Henry I know! That’s my favorite part of the apartment! Layla Henry, your new apartment is awesome! LIVING ENGLISH 22 Complete the mini dialogues with the expressions below. • Isn’t it great • I know • Oh, wow 1 A This is the yard. 2 A Your bedroom’s awesome! B ! B ! It’s really nice! ? 33 3.09 Listen and repeat the expressions. 6 3.08 Listen to the dialogue again. Then PRONUNCIATION practice with a partner. 4 3.10 Listen and repeat. 7 Role play a new dialogue. Follow the steps. Is it a table?  1 Change the words in blue to write a new dialogue in your notebook. What’s that?  2 Practice your dialogue with a partner. 3 Present your dialogue to the class. 35 3.11 Work in pairs. Read the questions. Then listen and check the pronunciation. Is there a yard?  Where’s the bedroom?  42 4 MILY UNIT GOALS FA MATTERS • T fa a m lk i l a ie b s o . ut people in • Read about different families. • Listen to two people talking about photos. • Learn about a family from Brazil. • Write a description of a family photo. VIDEO THINK! 4.1 1 What are two ways that people in 1 What is family? f 5 a .1 milies can be different? 2 Why is family important? 2 Say three reasons why family time is a happy time. 43 VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 4.01 Complete Tomas’s family tree with the words below. Then listen and check. • aunt • brother • dad • grandpa • sister My Family grandparents Lucia Martin grandma grandpa parents Antonia Jaime Renata Andres mom uncle Catalina Tomas Matias Pablo me cousin 44", "page": 47, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 19, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 4 2 4.02 Listen and repeat the family words. Say the family word and the name. grandma Lucía 3 Organize the family words in Exercise 1 in the chart below. LOOK! (informal) grandpa / grandma (formal) grandfather / grandmother (informal) dad / mom (formal) father / mother Male Female Both dad mom 4 Look at the family tree again. 5 Correct the sentences. Complete the sentences with 1 Catalina is Pablo’s sister. the words in Exercise 1. No, she’s not. She’s his cousin . 1 Who’s Jaime? 2 Andrés is Matias’s dad. He’s Tomas’s dad No, he’s not. He’s 2 Who’s Martin? . He’s Catalina’s . 3 Renata is Tomas’s mom. 3 Who’s Catalina? No, she’s not. She’s She’s Pablo’s . . 4 Antonia is Catalina’s aunt. 4 Who’s Antonia? No, she’s not. She’s She’s Matias’s . . 5 Who’s Jaime? 5 Antonia and Jaime are Tomas’s He’s Renata’s . grandparents. 6 Who’s Lucia? No, they’re not. They’re She’s Tomas’s . . 7 Who’s Catalina? She’s Matias’s . USE IT! 6 Write the names of fi ve people in your family. Then work in pairs. Ask and answer about your partner’s family members. Who’s Sara? Is she your sister? No, she’s my mom. Who’s Paolo? WORKBOOK p.21 4455 R WERAIDTIINNGG 1 Look at the text, the title and the images. Then check (✓) the correct answer and answer the question. 1 Where are these texts from? a class video presentation a class poster presentation 2 What are these texts about? OUR FAMILIES Hi! I’m Josh. Th is is my house ... and my grandma and Hi! My name’s Zoe. I have a brother, Taylor, but grandpa. Th ey’re my family. I have a cousin, Alex. Alex’s we’re from diff erent families: Taylor’s dad is not my home is in the United Kingdom. He has a big cat, called dad, and my mom is not Taylor’s mom. We’re a Suki, but they’re not here! So it’s my grandpa, my grandma, new family and we have a big house – it has four and me – three of us! Oh, and my two dogs, Pepe and Jaz. bedrooms! I have a very big family. Taylor has 23 Th ey have a small house in the yard! And that’s it. cousins, and I have 11! Together, we have 34 cousins! We have a small family! 2 4.03 Read and listen to the text. Find Josh and Zoe’s families. Tell J (Josh) or Z (Zoe). 1 2 3 Read the text again and choose the correct answers. 1 11 cousins Josh / Zoe 4 a small family Josh / Zoe 2 two dogs Josh / Zoe 5 a big family Josh / Zoe 3 one cousin Josh / Zoe 6 a grandma and Josh / Zoe a grandpa THINK! What types of families are there? 46", "page": 49, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 20, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 4 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples below. Complete the sentences from Josh and Zoe’s presentations. Verb to have Affi rmative (+) I, you, we, they he, she, it I have a cousin. He 23 cousins. You have a sister. We 34 cousins! She has a brother. They a small house in the yard! It four bedrooms. 2 Choose the correct verbs. LOOK! 1 My brother and I have / has a big family. There are fi ve 2 Miray have / has a brother called Samir. people in my family. 3 I have / has ten aunts and uncles, but I only have / has two cousins. I have two sisters. 4 My friend Sam have / has two sisters and they have / has a dog. 5 They’re a big family and they have / has a big house. It have / has seven bedrooms. 3 Look at the images and make sentences. Use has or have and the words below. • a sister • a brother • two cousins • a grandpa • a grandma 1 2 3 1 Leo and Felix have a sister. 2 He 3 We 4 5 4 Nina 5 I USE IT! I have eight cousins. 4 Make three sentences about your family. Tell them to your partner. 5 Make sentences about your partner’s family. Tell them to your class. Maria has eight cousins. WORKBOOK p.20, p.23 and p.24 4477 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 4.04 Name the images with the words below. Then listen, check, and repeat. • blue eyes • brown eyes • dark hair • fair hair • green eyes • long hair • short • short hair • tall 1 short 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 2 4.05 Listen to Mariana and Larissa and write the names of the people in the pictures in your notebook. • Luciana • Helena • Antonio • Gabi • Eduardo 3 1 2 3 Look at your answers above and complete the sentence. There are people in Mariana’s family. 4 4.05 Listen to Mariana and Larissa again and check (✓) the words that describe the people in the photos. brown eyes tall short fair hair dark hair long hair Luciana ✓ Antonio Gabi Helena Eduardo 48 WORKBOOK p.20 and p.21", "page": 51, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 21, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 4 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the questions and answers from the dialogue in the chart. Use the words below. • Do • Does • doesn’t • I do • she does Verb to have (I, you, he, she, we, they) Negative (-) Yes/No Questions Short Answers I don’t have a sister Do I have a sister? No, I don’t. You don’t have the photo. Do you have the photo? Yes, He/She doesn’t have blue eyes. he/she have blue eyes? No, he/she We don’t have long hair. Do we have long hair? Yes, we do. They don’t have green eyes. Do they have green eyes? No, they don’t. 22 Choose the correct verbs to complete the sentences. 1 I a big family. It’s my dad, my mom, and me. a have b don’t have 2 My mom a sister. Her name is Sabina. LOOK! a has b doesn’t have My family has seven 3 My cousins and I green eyes. They’re blue! members. a have b don’t have BUT 4 My dad any brothers or sisters. There are seven a has b doesn’t have members in my family. 3 Put the words in the correct order to make questions. Then answer them. 1 have / Does / dark / Isabella / hair / ? (X) Does Isabella have dark hair? No, she doesn’t. 2 you / eyes / Do / brown / have / ? (✓) 3 any / Michael / have / Does / cousins / ? (X) 4 Do / Alicia and Florence / long / have / hair / ? (X) USE IT! 4 Copy the chart to your notebook. Complete the questions and answer them so they are true for you. Mark (✓) or (X). Me My Partner Do you have dark hair? you have long hair? your mom have a brother or a sister? your dad have brown eyes? 5 Work in pairs. Ask and answer the questions. Mark (✓) or (X) in the chart for your partner. WORKBOOK p.20, p.22 and p.25 49", "page": 52, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 22, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "ACROSS THE CURRICULUM MATH The Saraíba Family By João Miguel Saraíba 6th Grade Teacher: Mrs. Capanema. Who are we? We’re a happy Brazilian family from the Amazon! In my house, it’s just my mom, my grandparents, my dog, and me. It’s not a very big family. But I have three uncles, and four aunts. My aunt Janaína is single. My other uncles and aunts are all married, and I have many cousins. I have 20 cousins. Six are from Parintins, like me, and four are from Barreirinha. My other cousins are from Santarém. All my cousins have brothers and sisters, but I don’t. I’m an only child, but it’s OK. I have my dog, Cupuaçu. That’s the name of my favorite fruit, too. My dog and me My cousin Uiara and me Cupuaçu fruit We love parties! My uncle Murici and my aunt Jacira have a big house in Paritins with cupuaçu and pupunha trees in the yard. We have family celebrations there. All our relatives and friends love our parties. We really have fun together, with a lot of Amazon food and music. And, of My aunt Jacira and her course, birthday cakes! birthday cake 50 UNIT 4 1 Look at João Miguel’s poster. Who is the audience? Check (✓) the correct answer. João Miguel’s family Mrs. Capanema and the students in his class the teacher and his mom young people on the Internet 2 4.06 Read and listen to the poster. Decide if the sentences are T (true) or F (false). 1 1/4 of João Miguel’s cousins are from Parintins. 2 50% of João Miguel’s cousins are from Santarém. 3 João Miguel has 19 cousins. 4 The cousins from Barreirinha have three brothers and sisters. 5 One cousin from Santarém is an only child. 3 Where are João Miguel’s cousins from? Check (✓) the correct chart. Barreirinhas Parintins Santarém 44 Read the poster again and answer the questions. 1 Where in Brazil is João Miguel’s family from? 4 Where are the family’s celebrations? the Amazon 2 Is João Miguel's dog part of the family? 5 What is there at the parties? 3 What is João Miguel's favorite fruit? WORDS IN CONTEXT 5 Match the words (1–4) with the definitions (a–d). 1 only child a celebration 2 party b family members 3 single c not married 4 relatives d person with no brothers or sisters THINK! Are your friends part of your family? VIDEO Why / Why not? 4.2 1 Where in the world are there big families? 2 Where in the world are there small families? 5511", "page": 54, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 23, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "W WRRIITTIINNGG 11 Look at the text. What is it? Check (✓) the correct answer. an email to a pen pal an online magazine article 16: 54 Bruno to me at 4:20 PM Hi! I’m Bruno. I’m tall and I have fair hair and green eyes, and this is my family. My parents are Amanda and Isaac. My mom is tall and has long, dark hair. My dad is tall, too. He has long, fair hair and brown eyes. My little sister is next to my mom. Her name’s Leticia. She’s short and has short, brown hair. Oh, my grandma Clara is not in the photo because she’s the photographer! 2 4.07 Read and listen to the text. Draw a chart in your notebook. Write the name of each person in Bruno’s family. Then complete the chart. Me! Bruno LOOK! He has long, fair hair. mom She has short, brown Isaac hair. Order of adjectives: sister style, color Clara 3 Write your description of your family to a pen pal. 1 Include a photo. 2 Introduce yourself. 3 Describe the people in the photo. 4 Change your description with a partner and check his/her work. Use the checklist. photo information about the people order of adjectives 52 REVIEW UNITS 3 AND 4 2 4 VOCABULARY 1 Look at the image. Number the parts of the house. 5 1 bathroom dining room 6 bedroom 1 kitchen living room yard 2 Look at the Oliveira’s family tree. Check (✓) the 3 correct sentences. Then correct the wrong one. 1 Juliana is Luis and Paula’s sister. 2 Leonardo is Henrique’s dad. 3 Mauro is Vitor’s grandpa. 4 Sandra is Ingrid’s grandma. Mauro Tereza Sandra Luis Paula Leonardo Juliana Luiza Ingrid Vitor Henrique 3 Look at the images and choose the correct words to complete the sentences. 1 2 3 4 Eliana has Luciana has Jacob has A Is Francisco brown / green eyes. short / long hair. blue / green eyes. short / tall? B Yes, he is. 4 Look at Nadia’s house and complete the sentences with There’s, There isn’t, There are, and There aren’t. 1 any chairs in the kitchen. 2 a window in the living room. 3 a closet in the bedroom. 4 pictures in the bathroom. 53", "page": 56, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 24, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 5 Complete the questions about Nadia’s house. Then answer them. 1 Is there a table in the kitchen? 3 a TV in the No, there isn’t. living room? 2 any chairs in the 4 any windows in living room? the bathroom? 6 Ask questions with the verb to have. Then answer them. 1 Luciano / a brother and two sisters? (✓) Does Luciano have a brother and two sisters? Yes, he does. 2 You / a dog and a cat? (X) 3 We / six uncles and eight aunts? (✓) 4 Your dad / a sister called / Debora? (X) 7 Complete the dialogue with the words below. • are there • do • has • have • there are • there aren’t • there’s Tomas Do you 1 have a big house? Priscilla Yes, I 2 . My family is big. 3 fi ve bedrooms in my house: one for my dad and my mom, one for my sisters Ana and Beatriz, one for me and my sister Juliana, and one for my Learn to learn brother Tiago. Tomas Wait … that’s four bedrooms. Priscilla Oh, right. 4 a bedroom for my grandma. And she 5 two cats, Lola and Nikita. Tomas 6 any dogs in your house? Priscilla No, 7 . Check your progress I CAN... • talk about parts of the It’s very important to look house and furniture. at new words every day. • use there is/there areto describe Write the new words from a home or a part of a house. your class on small pieces • talk about my family and of paper and put them in a their physical descriptions. jar. Choose one word from the jar every day, read it, and • use the verb to have to talk about my family. remember it! 54 5 AY D A UNIT GOALS IN THE • Talk about your daily routine. • Read a page from a LIFE student’s blog. • Listen to a podcast. • Learn about life in a circus. • Talk about your free time. THINK! VIDEO 5.1 Name the countries in the video. 1 What’s important in the girl’s daily routine? Are daily routines similar around 2 What’s important in your daily routine? the world? 55", "page": 58, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 25, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 1 5.01Complete Ivory’s video captions1 with the expressions below. Then listen and check your answers. • do my homework • get up • go home • go to bed • go to school • have breakfast • have dinner • play volleyball • take a shower • take the bus My Daily Routine! 1 2 At 6:30, I On school days, I get up at 6:00. with my family. 3 4 At 7:00, I I on Mondays with my brother. We . and Wednesdays. These are my favorite days! 5 6 I at 4:00 and I . Then I . 7 8 I with my brother and my mom. Finally, I . 1 A short text for a picture in a book or fi lm 56 UNIT 5 22 Complete the chart with the expressions in Exercise 1. In the morning In the afternoon In the evening Atnight play volleyball 33 Complete the chart with the expressions. • a pizza • a shower • breakfast • home • the bus • the subway • to bed • to school the train the bus a hamburger the bus the bus take have go the bus the bus the bus the bus the bus USE IT! 44 5.02 Listen and read. Check (✓) the sentences that are true for you. Me My Partner I do homework in the afternoon. I get up at 6:00 on Mondays. I have dinner with my family. I have lunch at 1:00. I take a shower in the morning. I take the bus to school. Work in pairs. Tell your partner your true sentences. Check (✓) the sentences your partner says. What’s your favorite time of day? Why? My favorite time of day is morning. WORKBOOK p.27 57", "page": 60, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 26, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING www.fresheyesfromsingapore.net Fresh Eyes HOME ABOUT PICTURES SCHOOL FROM SINGAPORE Hi! My name is Wei Jie, and I’m 14. I’m a student from Singapore. My passion is photography. I get up at 5:30 and I have breakfast. Then I take the MRT train to school with my friend Teo. Lessons start at 8:10, but before class, we work on math exercises. We fi nish school at 2:15. I don’t play sports. When I go home, I have lunch but I don’t rest. I do my homework and study until 8:00. Then I take a shower and have dinner with my parents. They ask a lot of questions! I chat online with friends. Then I study more. I like to watch TV series, but I don’t have time for that. I go to bed at 10:00. On Sundays, I don’t study! I take photos in the city and post them on my blog. I hope you like my photos! Sri Mariamman Temple Singapore Mass Rapid Transport (MRT) Shopping Mall 11 Look at the titles, images and design. Then answer the questions. 1 What type of text is this? an “about me” page on a blog a student’s school fi le 2 Who is the author? 3 What is her hobby? 22 5.03 Read and listen to the text and 3 Decide if the sentences are T (true) or F (false) for put the activities in chronological order. Wei Jie. 1 We work on math exercises. My Daily Routine Wei Jie Me I go home. 1 I study a lot! T I do homework and study. 2 I go to school with a friend. 3 I watch TV in the evening. I chat online. 4 I don’t do math in the morning. I have lunch. 5 I don’t play sports on weekdays. I take a shower. 6 I don’t have dinner with my parents. I go to bed. 4 What about you? Decide if the sentences are T We fi nish school. (true) or F (false) for you. THINK! School and homework are a big part of Wei Jie’s day. Is it good to study a lot like Wei Jie? Why? / Why not? 58", "page": 61, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 27, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 5 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 11 Look at the examples in the chart. Complete the sentences from Wei Jie’s blog. Simple Present (I, you, we, they) Affirmative (+) Negative (-) I get up at 5:30. On Sundays, I don’t study! I I to bed at 10:00. play sports. LOOK! at | 8:00 p.m. You do your homework. You don’t do your homework. | 10:15 a.m. They They don’t ask a lot of questions. on | Monday a lot of questions! | Tuesday | the weekend / We We don’t finish school at 4:00. weekdays school at 2:15. 22 Use the affirmative(+) or negative (-) forms of the verbs in parentheses. 1 We don’t take (take) the bus to school. We walk. (-) 2 I (have) lunch at school, then I go home. (+) 3 We (take) a shower in the morning. (+) 4 They (play) sports on weekdays. (-) 5 You (watch) TV in the evenings. (-) 33 Make true sentences about your routine. Use the affirmative (+) or negative (-) forms of the verbs. • take • chat • take • get up • have • get up 1 I get up at 5:30 on weekdays. 2 I at 5:30 on Sundays. 3 I the bus to school on Saturdays. 4 I a shower in the evening. 5 My parents dinner with me in the evening. 6 My friends and I online on weekends. WORKBOOK p.26, p.29 and p.30 59 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 11 Look at the image and check (✓) the correct answers. 1 What does it represent? an interview with a boy named Ramiro a song by Ramiro Bolaños 2 What’s the topic of the podcast with Ramiro? study life FREE TIME weekend activities Podcast for Teens 22 5.04 Listen to the podcast and check your answers. #13 – Ramiro Bolaños 33 5.05 Listen to the fi rst part of the podcast again and choose the correct options. 30s 30s 1 Ramiro is 12 / 13 years old. 2 He is from Guatemala / the USA. 3 Ramiro lives in Jalapa / Boston. 4 Ramiro’s weekends are fun / boring. 44 5.06 Listen to the rest of the podcast and check (✓) Ramiro’s free-time activities. 1 2 3 play video games watch movies play soccer 4 5 6 listen to music hang out with friends go to restaurants 60 WORKBOOK p.26 and p.27", "page": 63, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 28, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 5 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 11 Complete the chart with the words below. • do • do • do • don’t • don’t • play • what Simple Present (I, you, we, they) Yes/No Questions Short Answers Do you play soccer on Sundays? Yes, I do. Do we play sports? No, we . they watch TV on weekends? Yes, they do. they take the subway to school? No, they . Wh- Questions Answers What you do on weekends? I play volleyball and hang out with friends. time do you get up? I get up at 9:00 on weekends. Wheredo they have lunch? They have lunch at home. 22 Read the answers. Then put the words in the correct order to make questions. 1 our / homework / lunch / we / Do / do / after / ? 3 lunch / for / What / have / you / do / ? Yes, We do. We study for an hour. I have pizza. 2 shower / Do / a / take / in / you / morning / the / ? 4 do / Where / they / go / Sundays / on / ? No, I don’t. I take a shower in the evening. They go to their grandparents’ house. USE IT! 33 Complete the questions and answer with information about you. 1 What do you on weekday evenings? I . 2 Do you in the morning? . 3 Where on weekends? I . 4 Work in pairs. Ask and answer the questions. WORKBOOK p.26, p. 28 and p.31 61", "page": 64, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 29, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "AARROOUUNNDD TTHHEE WWOORRLLDD www.globalyouth.com NEWS SPORTS THE ARTS MAKE A DIFFERENCE PROFILES COMMENTS Youth Circus Life! by maxpadu | 9:50, July 10 Hi! I’m Anna, and I’m 14. I’m always in the air and on the road! I’m from Prague, the capital of the Czech Republic. I live in a trailer with my little brother Jan and our parents. Our trailer is part of a big circus caravan. We travel around Europe, and home is where the heart is! I don’t go to a regular school. My brother and I take classes with my parents in the morning. I have an online tutor, too. I also have a place in the trailer to study and keep my things. In the afternoon, I hang out with my friends in the circus and I practice my skills. I don’t have friends outside the caravan, but it’s OK. I meet new people in every town we stop in. I do juggling and aerial acrobatics. I practice seven days a week for four hours, but I don’t mind because I love acrobatics. In the evening, we do our show. Mom, Dad, Jan, and I do a family act together. I like my life because we’re free, and we do what we love. ONLINE COMMENTS Bunnie the bear Do you have animals in your circus? I hope not! It’s cruel. reply share Edward Hello. You don’t go to school? That’s so cool!! reply share preet preet Circuses are scary . I don’t know if it’s the clowns, or the music … I never go. reply share Your Comment: POST 62 UUNNIITT 55 11 Look at the text. Check (✓) all the elements that you see. a logo a title comments date headings for different parts of the text images 22 A text with these elements is probably … an online article. an online forum. an opinion article in a book. 33 5.07 Where is Anna from? Read and listen to the text. Check your answers. 44 Anna says, “I’m always in the air and on the road.” Why? Anna and her family fly to different places to do their show. Anna is part of a circus family and she and her family travel a lot. 55 What is it possible to say, based on the text? Check (✓) the correct answers. 1 Friends Anna and her friends spend time together. Anna is not happy because all her friends are from the circus. 2 Education Anna’s parents are responsible for her education. People in the circus don’t study regularly. 3 Work Anna and her family don’t work on weekends. Anna and her family work together in the circus. THINK! 1 Read the online comments. Write your opinion about the article in your notebook. 2 In your opinion, what’s the meaning of this sentence from the article: “Home is where the heart is”? VIDEO 5.2 1 I’m Mya. What time do I go to school? 2 What do I do in the evening? 6633", "page": 66, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 30, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "SPEAKING A Class Survey 11 5.08 Read and listen to Amelia and Noah. Amelia Hi, Noah! What do you do on Saturday Amelia Really?!? Do you like museums? afternoons? Noah Sure! How about you? Noah I play basketball with my friends. Amelia No way! Amelia Do you go out with your family? Noah Yes, I do. We go tothe park or a museum. LIVING ENGLISH • Sure! • Really? • No way! 22 Which expressions do they use to ... 1 show surprise? 2 say yes? 3 say no? 33 5.09 Listen and repeat the expressions. PRONUNCIATION Linking sounds: do you /dʒə/ Do you go out with your family? 44 5.10 LLiisstteenn aanndd rreeppeeaatt.. And what do you do on Saturday afternoons? 55 5.08 Listen to the dialogue again. Then practice with a partner. 66 Tell people about your free time activities. Follow the steps. 1 Change the words in blue to write a new dialogue in your notebook. 2 Practice your dialogue with a partner. 3 Present your dialogue to the class. 64 6 SCHOOL UNIT GOALS • Talk about school. E M TI • Read school notices. • Listen to a school radio program. • Learn about the planets in the solar system. • Write a class presentation. VIDEO THINK! 6.1 1 Which two things in the video do all Why is education important? 5.1students do at school? 2 List fi ve types of places from the video where students study. 65 VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 6.01 Look at Olivia’s schedule and listen. What’s Olivia’s favorite subject? 2 6.01 Listen again and complete the schedule with the words below. • history • math • music • PE • science • Spanish hhhhhhhh SCHOOL SUBJECTS uuuuu Monday Tuesday Wednesday 8:10–9:15 PE aarrtt 9:20–10:25 PE aarrtt Morning 10:25–10:40 BREAK ZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ 10:40–11:45 sscciieennccee English 11:45–12:30 LUNCH 12:30–1:35 geography English CCCCCCC computer Afternoon 1:40–2:45 geography science LLLLLLLLLLLLL computer 2:45–3:30 science 3:45–4:55 SPORTS CLUB SCIENCE CLUB ART CLUB mm 3 6.03 Listen to the sounds. What’s the subject? What day is it? 1 math Wednesday 2 3 4 5 66 4 Look at the school subjects and draw an emoji (like, love, don’t like, hate) for you. LIKE LOVE DON'T LIKE HATE Subject Me My Partner Subject Me My Partner math science art music history Spanish PE English geography 5 Look at the images. Make sentences with love, like, don’t like, and hate. 1 2 3 I love science. You I 4 5 We You USE IT! Do you like PE? No, I don’t! I hate PE! 6 Work in pairs. Ask and answer questions to complete the chart in Exercise 5 for your partner. Compare your answers. Do you like history? Yes, I do! 67 WORKBOOK p.33", "page": 70, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 31, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 1 Look at the image below. Check (✓) the information you can fi nd. ✓ days of the week teachers’ names places at school students’ names school subjects room number time school name 2 Look at the word in italics. What is it? Choose the correct option. It’s a school bulletin board / newspaper. rr r A AATTTTEENNTTIIOONN!! B MMUUSSIICC CCLLAASSSS AAllll Science Students CCoommee aanndd lliisstteenn ttoo tthhee bbaanndd.. Mr. Rothmann doesn’t teach science When? Wednesday r in a normal way – he works with What time? 4 p.m. projects! Come to the Science Project Where? The music classroom on Friday at 8 a.m. Don’t forget your lab clothes! Linda plays the guitar. Klaus plays Alec doesn’t play an instrument, C Are you a dog D PPrroobblleemmss wwiitthh mmaatthh?? the drums. but he’s a good singer! r oorr aa ccaatt PPEERRSSOONN?? CCoommee aanndd vviissiitt HHaannnnaahh,, Come and help at the animal our math expert. center! Craig, from 10th grade, helps at the animal center on On Tuesdays, she’s in Saturdays. Classroom 6 E SALE! More information? from 3 p.m. to 4 p.m. Each backpack costs $10! Contact She studies with students All colors, all designs. Craig Clinton and teaches them practical To order your new in Room 23, every day at 3 p.m. math tips. backpack, write to me at Become a math expert, like patibothamm@memail.com or text me at 555-9436. Hannah! 3 6.04 Read and listen to the texts. Which of the texts is good for the people below? Write the letters (A-E) in your notebook. 1 Ruben has problems with algebra. 4 Nozomi is at school at 4 p.m. on Wednesday. 2 Carol doesn’t have a school bag. 5 Jenny has a cat and is free on Saturdays. 3 Tom has new lab clothes. 4 Read the texts again and correct the sentences. 1 Mr. Rothmann is a music teacher. 4 The backpacks are $15. Mr. Rothmann is a science teacher. 2 The science project is on Thursday. 5 Hannah is a math student. 3 The music class is at 5 p.m. 6 Craig is at the animal center every day. THINK! What is the ideal schedule for you? 68", "page": 71, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 32, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 6 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples in the chart. Complete the sentences from the bulletin board. Simple Present (he, she, it) Affi rmative (+) Negative (-) Linda plays the guitar. He doesn’t play an instrument. Craig at the animal center. He teach science in a normal way. Hannah with students. She doesn’tstudy on Mondays. Each backpack $10. It doesn’tcost $20. 2 Choose the correct verbs to complete the sentences. 1 Hannah doesn’t to Classroom 4 Pati colored backpacks. 6 on Saturdays. a sell b sells a go b goes 5 Hannah doesn’t English 2 Klaus in the band. a teach b teaches a play b plays 3 Mr. Rothmann to Classroom 2 for the science project on Friday. LOOK! a go b goes read – reads sell – sells 3 Complete the sentences. Use the correct form of the verbs. wash – washes 1 Craig stays (stay) in Room 23 at 3 p.m. play – plays stay – stays 2 Klaus (not read) at 4 p.m. on Wednesday. teach – teaches 3 Lisa (study) with Hannah in Classroom 6. go – goes study – studies 4 Alec (not play) guitar. 5 Pati (not sell) old backpacks. 6 Craig (help) at the animal center. USE IT! 4 Work in pairs. Ask and answer questions about school. M ark (✓) or (X) in the chart. My Partner Do you get up at 7 a.m. on school days? get up at 7 a.m. on school days have English class every day go to school on Saturday No, I don’t. / Yes, I do. hate math love geography like music WORKBOOK p.32,p.35 and p.36 69 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 6.05 Listen to a school radio program. What is it about? Check (✓) the correct option. new popular songs school activities new teachers 2 6.05 Listen to the school radio program again. Number the school places below (1–9) with the diagram. 7 athletic fi eld cafeteria gymnasium library maker lab principal’s offi ce restrooms science lab teachers’ lounge 1 6 9 7 2 5 8 4 3 3 6.06 Listen, check, and repeat. 4 6.05 Listen again and match the beginnings of the sentences (1–5) with the endings (a–e). 1 Aaron is in the a maker lab. 2 Students work with robots in the b athletic fi eld. 3 The maker lab is by the c teachers’ lounge. 4 Read your favorite authors in the d cafeteria. 5 Soccer practice is at the e library. THINK! 1 Do you have a school radio station in your school? 2 Is it a good idea to have one? Why? / Why not? 70 WORKBOOK p.32 and p.33", "page": 73, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 33, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 6 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the questions and answers from the radio program in the chart. Use the words below. • Does • Does • does • does • doesn’t • have Simple Present (he, she, it) Yes/No Questions Short Answers he speak? No, he . Does she like robots? Yes, she does. it have a 3-D printer? Yes, it . Wh- Questions Answers Where does he do projects? He does projects in the maker lab. When it open? It opens at 8 a.m. What does the library have? It has books! 2 Answer the questions. 1 A Does Grayson ride his bike to school? B No, he doesn’t. He takes the bus. 2 A Does Kaylee watch videos before bed? B No, . She books. 3 A Does Amelia have lunch at the school cafeteria? B No, .She lunch at home. 4 A Does Elijah take science lab classes? B Yes, . 3 Ask questions. 1 Maria / like / robots 3 Clara / chat online / in the morning Does Maria like robots? 2 Zak / get up / at six o’clock / on weekends 4 Eliot / take the bus / to school / every day USE IT! What do you do in the evening? 4 Complete the chart so it is true for you. Then work in pairs. Ask and answer the I play volleyball. questions and complete the chart with your partner’s answers. Me My Partner What do / in the evening have math / Tuesday Where go / after school 5 Change partners. Ask and answer the questions about different students. Does Maria have math on Tuesday? Yes, she does. WORKBOOK p.32, p.34 and p.37 71 ACROSS THE CURRICULUM SCIENCE www.highlight.com g g hL h i t H i What do you know about Jupiter? By Mia Stone Marvin Oatsmann from 7th grade is our school’s participant in this year’s National Science Fair in Baltimore. Read the interview and learn more about Marvin and his work. Congratulations, Marvin! Do you join our school’s science fair every year? Thanks! Yes, I do! I think participation is very important. I’m crazy about science classes. Your work this year is about Jupiter. Why? Well, I like everything about the solar system and the planets, and Jupiter is a very special planet. It’s a gas giant made of hydrogen and helium. Is it possible to see Jupiter from Earth? Sure! When you look at the sky at night you see the moon, you see Venus, and you see Jupiter, too! That’s fantastic! What other things are interesting about Jupiter? Oh, so many things ... Jupiter has 79 moons, and it has rings, too, similar to the rings of Saturn. And there’s the Great Red Spot, a great storm in the atmosphere of the planet. Wow, awesome! Thank you, Marvin, and good luck at the National Science Fair! Thank you! 72", "page": 75, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 34, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 6 1 Look at the text title, design, and images. What type of text is it? Check (✓) the correct answer. a blog post an interview in a newspaper a discussion in an online forum 2 Read the title. What is the main topic of the text? Check (✓) the correct answer. a description of the planets how to participate in a science fair information about Jupiter 3 6.07 Read and listen to the text. Check (✓) the correct answers. 1 Marvin Oatsmann ... 3 The school science fair ... studies in a school in Baltimore. happens every year at the school. likes 7th grade science classes very much. is about Jupiter this year. 2 Marvin’s work ... is about Jupiter’s moons. represents his school in the National Science Fair. 4 Read the text again and answer the questions. 1 What do you see in the sky at night? 3 What is the Great Red Spot? 2 Does Jupiter have 77 moons? 4 Does Saturn have rings? WORDS IN CONTEXT 5 Answer the sentences with the expressions below. • Congratulations! • Good luck! A I have a diffi cult soccer game on Friday B MMyy rreeppoorrtt ccaarrdd tthhiiss yyeeaarr hhaass tteenn ‘‘AA’’ss.. at school. I hope we win. 6 Find expressions in the text that are similar to the expressions below. 1 bad weather, like a tornado or hurricane 2 I really like ... 3 Of course! THINK! Is there a science fair in your school? VIDEO Do you participate? Why / Why not? 6.2 1 How many planets are in our solar system? 2 Which planet is really hot? 7733", "page": 76, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 35, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "WRITING 1 2 3 This is it! At my ideal school, we We don’t study history , My Ideal School study art , music , and math . geography , or science ! (I love math!) 4 5 It has a cafeteria – we eat 6 We use our cell phones hamburgers, pizzas, and ketchup! What’s your ideal school? Does it when we like! There’s a gymnasium for all have cool things? Bye! sports, and a library. Books are awesome! It doesn’t have a science lab – I don’t like science! LOOK! In the presentations, 1 6.08 Read and listen to the presentation. Answer the questions. use icons to help people understand 1 How many words are there on each slide? your message. Slide 1: 3 Slide 2: Slide 3: Slide 4: Slide 5: Slide 6: 2 Do the images represent the ideas in the text? 2 Put the slide numbers in the correct place in the chart. Title Introduction Information Conclusion Slide 1 3 Plan a presentation about your ideal school. 4 Change presentations with a partner and check his/her work. Use the checklist below. 1 Think about the subjects you study and the number of slides places in a school. title, introduction, information, and conclusion 2 Make short notes on each slide. number of words in each slide 3 Write the fi rst version of your presentation. images icons 74", "page": 77, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 36, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "REVIEW UNITS 5 AND 6 VOCABULARY 1 Match the beginnings of the sentences (1–4) with the endings (a–d). 1 I get up at a restaurant on Sundays. 2 I have dinner at a b homework in the afternoon. 3 I take a shower c 9 a.m. on weekends. 4 I do my d in the evening. 2 Complete the sentences with the words below. • video games • friends • movies • music 1 Susanna plays video games with her friends. Her favorite is Super Mario. 2 Arthur and Dylan watch on weekends. 3 Lola listens to in the evening. 4 I like to hang out with my on Saturdays. 3 Look at the images and choose the correct words. 1 2 3 4 I like PE / math. I hate science / music. I don’t like math / art. I love science / history! 4 Read the questions and answer them. Where do you go to ... 1 clean your hands? 2 have lunch? 3 talk to a teacher? 4 read a book? restroom 5 Make affirmative (+) and negative (-) sentences. 1 We / do / homework / on weekdays / (-) 3 Debbie / take / a shower / in the evening / (+) We don’t do homework on weekdays. 2 They / have dinner / at home / on Fridays / (+) 4 Edmond / play / soccer / at school / (-) 6 Ask questions and give short answers. 1 you / take the bus to school / (+) 3 your parents / help at the animal center / (+) Do you take the bus to school? Yes, I do. 2 your friend / have lunch at home / (+) 4 your teacher / play the guitar / (-) 75", "page": 78, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 37, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 7 Ask questions for the underlined words in the answers. 1 Where do you have lunch with your parents? 3 I have lunch with my parents at home. They play volleyball with their friends on weekends. 2 4 She gets up at 7 a.m. I listen to music in the evening. 8 Complete Jason's routine with the verbs below. • get up • watch • have (3x) • not take • take (2x) • play • not do Hi! I’m Dale, and this is my friend, Jason. He’s a student. He 1 gets up at 6 a.m. and he 2 breakfast with his family. He 3 the train to school – he 4 the bus. He 5 lunch at school. Then he 6 soccer in the afternoon. He goes home at 5 p.m., but he 7 his homework. He 8 TV! He 9 dinner, 10 a shower, and then he goes to bed. 9 Write about your weekend. Use the phrases below and the affi rmative and negative forms of the verbs. • get up • have breakfast / lunch / dinner • do homework • hang out with friends • go to the park / museum • go to bed Check your progress I CAN... • talk about routines and free-time activities. • use the simple present to discuss routines and free-time activities. • talk about school subjects and places at school. • use the simple present in third person to describe activities at school. Learn to learn My dictionary Write an example sentence with new words. breakfast = I have breakfast with my family. Draw a picture too! breakfast = 76 7 UNIT GOALS WHAT'S HE • Talk about clothes. WEARING? • R fri e e a n d d s a . chat between two • Listen to a friend describing his sister. • Learn about the Bedouins. • Talk about an image of someone’s clothes. THINK! VIDEO 7.1 “You are what you wear.” Do you agree? 1 How are Tokyo and London similar? 2 What two things does the video talk about that affect our clothing choices? 77 VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 7.01 Match the images with the words below. Then listen, check, and repeat. • jacket • pants • shoes • shorts • sweatshirt • T-shirt www.teenfashion.com online webstore log in FIND A STORE | GIFT CARD SEARCH CLOTHES 1 2 3 sweatshirt a big red blue jeans a black 4 55 6 green white white sneakers 77 8 9 a red and blue shirt a blue black 78", "page": 81, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 38, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 7 2 Which clothes in the photos in Exercise 1 do you like? Tell your partner. I l ike the jeans! I love the …! I hate the … 3 Find the odd one out. 1 jeans / pants / sweatshirt 2 T-shirt / sneakers / shirt 3 shorts / jacket / sweatshirt 4 jacket / pants / shorts 5 shoes / sneakers / shirt USE IT! 4 Copy the chart to your notebook. Write the names of clothes you wear in the chart. Then tell your partner. Clothes I Wear at School Clothes I Wear on Weekends I wear shoes at school. I wear sneakers on weekends. 5 What are your favorite clothes? Tell your partner. My favorite clothes are my sneakers and sweatshirt. WORKBOOK p.39 79 READING 1 Look at the page and answer the questions. Check (✓) the correct answers. 1 What type of text is it? a cell phone dialogue between two friends an online blog post 2 What is the relationship between the two people? They’re brothers. They’re friends. 2 7.02 Read and listen to the text and check your answers to Exercise 1. Hey, Jordan. What’s up? Why not? Wait, what about a black T-shirt? Hi, Nick! I’m at the mall with my dad and my sister. My dad is getting a I don’t have one. shirt for work and a sweatshirt for the weekend. My sister is getting a sweatshirt, too. They’re buying the I have one. Wear it to the party! ssaammee oonnee!! II’’mm bbuuyyiinngg aa nneeww ppaaiirr ooff jeans and a new T-shirt for Jackson’s party. Cool! Thanks, Jordan! WWhhyy?? YYoouu hhaavvee lloottss ooff TT--sshhiirrttss!!!! I’m wearing my black jacket and my sneakers. You’re right. I’m not buying it! I’m not wearing my sneakers. I’m I’m in the store, but it’s closing wearing my blue shoes. Come to now. Where are you? mmmyyy hhhooouuussseee aaafffttteeerrr sssooocccccceeerrr cccllluuubbb tttooo gggooo to the party. I’m at home. I’m looking at my clothes for the party. I like the brown pants. But I’m not wearing my favorite white T-shirt. 3 Look at the emojis in the text. Draw the emoji for each adjective. 1 happy 2 sad 3 good 4 think 4 Read the text again. Then complete the text below with the correct words. Jordan is at the mall with his 1 dad and his sister. Nick is at 2 . They’re talking about 3 party. Jordan is in a 4 , but he doesn’t buy a 5 because he has lots of them. Nick is wearing brown 6 , Jordan’s 7 T-shirt, and a jacket to the party. Jordan isn’t wearing 8 . THINK! Is it important to look good? Why / Why not? 80", "page": 83, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 39, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 7 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples in the chart. Complete the sentences from Nick and Jordan’s chat. Present Progressive Affi rmative (+) Negative (-) I’m looking at my clothes. I’m not looking at my clothes. You’re wearing your blue shoes. You’re not wearing your sneakers. We’re buying pants. We’re not buying pants. They ’re buying the same one. They’re not buying the same one. LOOK! He’s a shirt. He’s not getting a shirt. Use wear with She’s a sweatshirt. She’s not getting a sweatshirt. clothes. It now. It’s not closing now. I’m wearing black shoes. 2 Use the words to make sentences. She’s wearing new pants. 1 Gunay / blue jacket (✓) 4 Emil / blue jeans (X) Gunay is wearing a blue jacket . . She's not wearing a red jacket. He's white jeans. 2 Mark / blue shorts (✓) 5 Anna / white sneakers (✓) . . He's black shorts. She's black shoes. 3 Ingrid / red T-shirt (X) . She's red shirt. 3 Nick and Jordan are at Jackson’s party. What are they wearing? Make sentences. Nick Jordan USE IT! I’m wearing blue pants, a green T-shirt … 4 Work in pairs. You’re at a party with Nick and Jordan. Describe what you are wearing. WORKBOOK p.38, p.41 and p.42 8811 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 Match the sentences (1–6) with the images (A–F). A B C D E F 1 She’s wearing a hat and glasses. 4 She’s wearing glasses, a hat, jeans, and a top. 2 She’s wearing a skirt and socks. 5 She’s wearing a jacket, jeans, and a hat. 3 She’s wearing a dress and glasses. 6 She’s wearing black boots, a coat, and a black hat. 2 7.03 Put the letters in the correct order to make clothes words. Then listen, check and repeat. 1 pot top 4 skcso 7 riskt 2 tosbo 5 atco 8 segssla 3 dsser 6 ath 3 7.04 Look at the images in Exercise 1 and listen to the dialogue. Who is Sergio’s sister? Complete the sentence. Sergio’s sister is the girl in picture . 4 7.04 Listen to the dialogue again and choose the correct answers. 1 Carlos is waiting / not waiting for Sergio by the movie theater. 2 Sergio’s sister is wearing / not wearing a hat. 3 Carlos is wearing / not wearing glasses. 4 Carlos is wearing / not wearing a coat. 5 Sergio’s sister is waiting / not waiting for Sergio by the cafeteria. 82 WORKBOOK p.38 and p.39", "page": 85, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 40, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 7 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the questions and answers from the dialogue in the chart. Use the words below. • ’m • are (2x) • Is • waiting • wearing (3x) Present Progressive Yes/No Questions Short Answers Am I meeting at the movie theater? Yes, I am. No, I ’m not. you your glasses? Yes, you are. No, you’renot. Are we waiting by the library? Yes, we are. No, we’renot. Are they meeting in the cafeteria? Yes, they are. No, they’renot. Is he wearing jeans? Yes, he is. No, he’s not. she for me in the cafeteria? Yes, she is. No, she’snot. Is it opening now? Yes, it is. No, it’snot. Wh- Questions I’m my jeans, a green What you ? top and green socks. 2 Ask questions and answers with the words below. 1 They / play volleyball (X) / listen to music (✓) 4 Carlos / buy jeans (X) / look at T-shirts (✓) Are they playing volleyball? No, they’re not. They’re listening to music. 2 Julie / go to bed (X) / do her homework (✓) 5 Emma, Jo, and Liz / have dinner (X) / have lunch (✓) 3 Tom and his dad / play soccer (X) / play video games (✓) LOOK! They’re meeting in the cafeteria now / right now / at this moment. (at the time of speaking) 3 Ask questions and answer them for you. 1 What / wear? 2 What / your teacher / do? 3 What / your best friend / do / now? USE IT! 4 Work in pairs. Ask and answer the questions in Exercise 3. Then compare your answers. WORKBOOK p.38, p.40 and p.43 83 AROUND THE WORLD CLOTHES FOR THE EXTREME How to dress in the Every month we have a new article dd ee ss ee rr tt about clothes and culture. This month we’re talking to Ahmad Mostafa. My name is Ahmad Mostafa abu-Rabia Sulaym, In this picture, my and I’m a 13-year-old Bedouin brother Abdulah is next from the Arabian desert. I’m an to one of our camels. But wait ... artist, and I’m sending two of my Is Abdulah wearing a dress? Yes, he pictures. Th ey show the type of is, because it’s very hot in the desert clothes that we wear in our so we wear loose clothes. We all wear community. dresses: women, girls, boys, and men. He’s not wearing a hat on his head, but a ghutra. Th is protects his head from the sun. He’s wearing sandals, too, because the sand is really hot. And what are the people doing in this picture? It’s the end of the day, and the men are sitting and listening to traditional stories. Some are wearing coats, or furwahs, because the nights are cold. Who is the woman wearing a black dress? And what is she doing? Well, that’s my aunt Aisha, and she’s working. She’s bringing water to the camp. TTeeeenn WWoorrlldd 3366 84", "page": 87, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 41, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 7 1 Look at the article, the titles, and the images. Then answer the question. Check (✓) the correct answer. What do you think the article is about? families and traditions in the desert water in the desert people’s clothes in the desert 2 Read the article quickly. Check (✓) the words in the article. dress glasses pants jacket coat clothes 3 7.05 Read and listen to the article. Check your answers to Exercises 1 and 2. 4 Match the beginnings of the sentences (1–4) with the endings (a–d). 1 Ahmad a is working. 2 Abdulah b is sending his pictures to the magazine. 3 The men c are sitting and listening to stories. 4 Aisha d is wearing a dress and a ghutra. 5 Read the article again. Decide if the sentences are T (true) or F (false). 1 Abdulah is an artist. F 2 In the desert, women wear dresses and men wear pants. 3 Hats are common to protect from the desert sun. 4 Sandals protect your feet from the hot sand. 5 Nights are always hot in the desert. 6 Bedouin women are responsible for getting water. WORDS IN CONTEXT 6 Complete the sentences with the words below. • cold • hot • sandals • loose • sand 1 People wear coats to protect them from temperatures. 2 The Bedouins usually wear clothes, because it’s hot in the desert. 3 People wear in the summer, not shoes or sneakers. 4 The in the desert is very hot and it’s difficult to walk there. 5 People don’t wear coats when it’s . THINK! Do clothes reflect our personality and culture? VIDEO 7.2 1 Which places can you see in the video? 2 What are your favorite clothes in the video? 85", "page": 88, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 42, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "SPEAKING GIVING OPINIONS 1 7.06 Read and listen to two friends talking about clothes. Where are they? Lucca Hi, Georgia. Are you wearing a new sweatshirt? Georgia Yeah. It’s my brother’s. Do you like it? Lucca Um … not really. I prefer your red sweatshirt. Georgia Well, that’s my favorite. But this sweatshirt is nice. Lucca Hmmm, I guess it’s a bit big. Georgia Really? Lucca Yes, and I think it’s really old. Georgia You’re right! Lucca What are you doing? Georgia I’m changing my sweatshirt! LIVING ENGLISH 2 Complete the mini dialogues with the expressions below. • I prefer • Not really • I guess 1 3 A Do you like my new sneakers? A Do you like my pants? B No, your old ones. B – sorry. I don’t like 2 green pants. A Where’s my new sweater? B I don’t know. In the closet, . 3 7.07 Listen and repeat the expressions. PRONUNCIATION This is my brother’s sweatshirt. You’re right. 4 7.08 Listen and repeat. 5 7.06 Listen to the dialogue again. Then practice with a partner. 6 Role play a new dialogue. Follow the steps. 1 Take a picture of your friend in nice clothes. 2 Change the words in blue to write a new dialogue in your notebook. 3 Practice your dialogue with a partner. 4 Present your dialogue to the class. 86 8 UNIT GOALS ET G • Talk about sports. MOVING! • R an e d a d s p a o b r o ts u . t people • Listen to a podcast. • Learn about why we do sports. • Write an email. THINK! VIDEO 8.1 5.1 1 Who can do sports? What sports do you like? 2 Say two things that sport can teach us. 87 VOCABULARY IN CONTEXT 1 8.01 Choose the correct verbs to complete the poster. Then listen and check your answers. SSSSppppoooorrrrttttssss 1 Swim / dance or surf / run 2 Ice-skate / Play volleyball or run / surf in the ocean with your friends. on the beach. ome to Andalusia, Spain to do sports! 3Swim / skiin the mountains! 5And in the evening, dance / ski to great music with your friends! 4Ice-skate / play volleyballat the ice rink. 88 UNIT 8 2 Organize the verbs below in the circles. Do you use your hand or foot? • kick • throw • catch • walk • run kick 3 8.03 Match the images with the words in Exercise 2. Then listen, check, and repeat. 1 2 3 4 5 USE IT! 4 What sports do you do? Mark (✓) or (X). 5 Work in pairs. Ask and answer the questions. Mark (✓) or (X) for your partner. Me My Partner ski run What sports do you do? dance play basketball I dance, I run, and I swim. surf I don’t surf or ski. ice-skate swim WORKBOOK p.45 89", "page": 92, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 43, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 1 Look at the text and the images. Then check (✓) the correct answer and answer the question. 1 What type of text is this? a blog about athletes a pamphlet with recommendations 2 Who is your favorite athlete? Why? www.sportschamps.com 3 comments Theo Curin is from France. He swims in the Paralympics. He swims for four hours Max Max I love Saki! She’s a day, and on weekends, he swims in awesome. I can kick a ball competitions. He can swim very fast, but very hard, but I can’t play volleyball. he can’t ski or ice-skate. reply Julia Wow! Théo is my hero. I Saki Kumagaiis a Japanese soccer player, can swim 100 meters in but she plays for a French team. She loves three minutes, but I can’t soccer, but she likes other sports too, like swim fast like Théo! basketball and volleyball. She can kick the ball very hard, but she can’t swim very reply well. Helena I run every day for two hours. I can run fast, but Clarence Munyaiis from South Africa. Clarence is great! He can He lives with his mom and dad, his run 100 meters in about 10 three sisters, and his brother. He can run seconds. I can’t! very fast! He can run 200 meters in 20 seconds! He can play soccer, but he can’t reply dance. 2 8.04 Read and listen to the text. Check (✓) the correct person in the chart. Theo Saki Clarence kick the ball very hard run very fast swim very well swim very fast play basketball play soccer 3 Read the text again and answer the questions. 1 What does Theo do? 4 Who does Clarence live with? Theo swims. 2 Where is Saki from? 5 Does Clarence play soccer? 3 What are Saki’s favorite sports? 6 Who can swim 100 meters in 180 seconds? THINK! Are sports important? Why / Why not? 90", "page": 93, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 44, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 8 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Look at the examples in the chart. Complete the sentences from the blog. Can: Ability Affi rmative (+) Negative (-) I can run fast. I can’t run fast. LOOK! He play soccer. He dance. can’t = cannot She kick the ball. She swim. I can’t play It can dance. It can’t dance. volleyball. I cannot play We can dance. We can’t dance. volleyball. You can ski. You can’t ski. They can play volleyball. They can’t play volleyball. 2 Complete the sentences with can or can’t and the verbs in parentheses. 1 I can play (play ✓) volleyball. 4 They (eat X) pizza. 2 He (walk X) to school. 5 You (dance ✓) very well. 3 She (surf ✓) in the ocean. 6 We (ice-skate X) today. Yes/No Questions Short Answers Yes, I/you/he/she/it/we/they can. Can I/you/he/she/it/we/they dance? No, I/you/he/she/it/we/they can’t. 3 Ask questions and answer about what Marta and Luis can and can’t do. play volleyball run fast dance 1 Marta X ✓ ✓ 2 Luis ✓ ✓ X 1 Can Marta play volleyball? No, she can’t. Can Luis play volleyball? Yes, he can. 2 Marta and Luis 3 Marta Luis USE IT! 4 Write questions for your partner with can and the words below in your notebook.. • dance • run fast • ice-skate • spell your name • play soccer • swim Can you dance? 5 Ask and answer the questions with your partner. Can you dance? No, I can’t. WORKBOOK p.44, p.47 and p.48 91 LISTENING AND VOCABULARY 1 Look at the image and check (✓) the correct answer. What does it represent? an infographic an interview 2 8.05 Look at the image. Complete the sentences with the words below. Then listen to the podcast and check. • do exercise • don’t eat junk food • don’t go to bed late • don’t sit down all day • drink water • eat healthy food NO ENERGY? Do Include 60 exercise minutes Don’t take of activity the bus Kick a soccer ball Walk with your friends Play Don’t drink Go to bed basketball soda early! Hang out with your friends Catch a volleyball COME ON! YOU CAN DO IT! 3 Complete the chart with expressions that have similar meanings. Use the infographic to help you. Do exercise. 1 Don’t sit down all day. 2 Don’t eat junk food. Go to bed early. 3 4 Don’t drink soda. 4 8.06 Listen, check, and repeat. 5 8.07 Listen to Maria and Sergio. Check (✓) what they do. Maria Sergio play basketball ✓ eat junk food eat healthy food play on the cell phone do exercise 92 WORKBOOK p.44 and p.45", "page": 95, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 45, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 8 LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 1 Complete the instructions from the podcast in the chart. Use the words below. • Put • Don’t eat • Go • Come • Don’t take Imperatives Affi rmative (+) Negative (-) Put on your sneakers. the bus to school. to the park. junk food. Don’t drink soda! on! 2 Match the beginnings of the sentences (1–6) with the endings (a–f). 1 Don’t write a your homework every day. 2 Don’t forget b to drink two liters of water every day. 3 Eat c your cell phone in class. 4 Do d on the wall! 5 Get up e now. It’s ten o’clock! 6 Don’t use f fruit to be healthy! 3 Look at the images. Make affi rmative and negative imperative sentences. • eat • go to bed late • run • watch TV • wear my T-shirt ! 1 Run ! 2 5 ! 3 ! 4 USE IT! Catch a ball! Drink water! 4 Work in pairs. Give instructions and act them out. WORKBOOK p.44, p.46 and p.49 93 AACCRROOSSSS THE CURRICULUM PHYSICAL EDUCATION But for scientists, sports are really good Children for you play sports because they can have fun with their friends, they feel good playing, and they like to compete. Scientists say sports can ... • increase muscle strength. • reduce stress, depression, and extra weight. • improve focus, memory, and school work. • teach teamwork and respect. Sports like running, soccer, and swimming develop your heart and lungs. SSoo,, ttoo bbee healthy and strong, add 60 Yoga and Pilates minutes of sports to are excellent for your day, and go for it: fl exibility. you can try different types of sports, And activities like practice every day, weight training can and enjoy life! make you strong. SportsActive.org orts for p D S i f n t f e r e e r n e t f f i B D e n e f i t s physically. emotionally, mentally, and socially. Scientists also say that it’s good to practice different types of sports, not only one. Why? When you play different sports that have a variety of movements and skills, you feel motivated. Different sports develop different physical abilities. 94", "page": 97, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 46, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "UNIT 8 1 Read the text quickly and check (✓) the correct answer. 1 The aim of the text is ... to ask children to take part in physical education classes. to inform about multiple benefits of sports. to tell a story with attractive images and lettering. 2 You can say that the text is ... artistic. critical. educational. 2 8.08 Read and listen to the text. Check (✓) the true sentences. All children play sports. Scientists do lots of sports. All sports develop the same physical skills. Sports are fun. It’s a good idea to practice different sports. 3 What are the activities below good for? Read the text again and complete the chart. • running • Pilates • soccer • swimming • weight training • yoga Cardio Activity Flexibility Strength running, 4 Match the beginnings of the sentences (1–5) with the endings (a–e). 1 Different sports can develop different a collaboration and respect. 2 To be flexible, b physical abilities. 3 Practice sports for 60 minutes a day c do yoga and Pilates. 4 Scientists say that sports are good for you d physically, mentally, and socially. 5 Sports can teach e to be healthy and strong. WORDS IN CONTEXT 6 Complete the sentences with the words below. 5 Find in the text … • develop • strength • strong • weight training 1 the opposite of “reduce”: 1 makes your 2 a synonym for “abilities”: muscles big. 3 a word for “to make something better”: 2 Exercise makes you healthy and . 3 Damien does different sports. He wants to new physical skills. 4 Djamila has the to win a gold medal at the Olympics. THINK! VIDEO Do you think these types of texts are effective 8.2 1 How many sports can you to motivate people? Why / Why not? remember from the video? 2 Where is the mermaid swimming? 9955", "page": 98, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 47, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "WRITING From: samhans@youmail.com To: pesmith@youmail.com Subject: PE classes 1 2 Dear Mr. Smith, 3 I’m Sam and I’m writing to you to suggest a new activity for our PE class. My favorite sport is basketball. This is a good activity for our PE class because we can become strong, develop our muscles, and work with coordination. Basketball is an activity that we can do in the gymnasium. It’s a good activity because we can improve teamwork and have fun. 4 Best wishes, Sam 1 8.09 Read and listen to the email and answer the questions. 1 Who is writing the email? 2 Who is receiving the email? 2 What’s the main idea in the email? to propose basketball as a PE activity to express all the students’ opinions to show how PE classes can be fun 3 Number the parts of the email from 1–4. greeting closing introduction subject 4 Read the Look! box. Underline examples of because in the email. LOOK! Use because to give 5 Plan an email, giving your suggestion for a new activity in PE classes. a reason why. I’m writing to you 1 Think about the activities you like. because … 2 Use Sam’s email as a model to plan your text. 3 Write the fi rst version of your email. Make sure you include the parts of an email in Exercise 3. 6 Change presentations with a partner and check his/her work. Use the checklist below. name of person sending the email name of person receiving the email greeting introduction and suggestion for a new activity subject closing 96 REVIEW UNITS 7 AND 8 VOCABULARY 1 Match the sentences (1–4) with the images (A–D). A B C D 1 This is my favorite coat. It’s nice! 3 I like informal clothes. This sweatshirt is cool. 2 I’m wearing a red shirt. I love it! 4 I’m wearing my new pants. They’re great. 2 Look at the images. What do you wear in the situations below? 1 2 3 3 Find the odd one out. 1 surf / swim / dance 2 run / iceskate / ski 3 volleyball / surf / soccer 4 top / boots / socks 4 Complete the sentences. 1 Don’t drink soda. 3 exercise. 2 to bed late. 4 junk food. 5 Make sentences with the information in parentheses. 1 I’m wearing a T-shirt. (- / shirt) I’m not wearing a T-shirt. I’m wearing a shirt. 2 She’s not wearing boots. (+) 3 They’re wearing shorts. (- / jeans) 4 We’re not wearing white T-shirts. (+) REVIEW 97", "page": 100, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 48, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "LANGUAGE IN CONTEXT 6 Choose the correct answers. 1 Are you and Greg meeting in the cafeteria? a Yes, they are. b No, we’re not. 2 What are you wearing? a I’m wearing jeans. b I’m at the library. 3 Are they wearing their glasses? a Yes, they are. b No, we’re not. 4 Are you listening to music? a No, I’m doing homework. b Yes, I’m playing video games. 7 Read the chart and make sentences about what the people can and can’t do in your notebook. kick a ball catch a ball play soccer throw a ball Amina ✓ X ✓ Dylan ✓ X Bella ✓ X ✓ Xavier X ✓ X 1 Amina can kick a ball and play soccer, but she can’t catch a ball. 2 3 4 8 Ask questions. Then answer the questions so they are true for you. 1 play soccer 3 ice-skate Can you play soccer? No, I can’t. 2 throw a ball 4 dance 9 Look at the pictures and make sentences. 1 2 3 4 ✓✓ XX ✓✓ XX Drink water. Check your progress Learn to learn I CAN... Vocabulary Categorizati on • talk about clothes. You can categorize groups of words with other words, for example, kick, throw, catch, walk, • use the present progressive and run. Use them with the nouns hand and to describe clothes. foot to help you remember them. • talk about sports and skills. • use can and imperatives to say what people can do. 98 REVIEW R E G N A H C E M A G EXTRAS READING 1 MATH: A CLASS SURVEY PAGE 100 READING 2 UNUSUAL HOMES PAGE 101 READING 3 GEOGRAPHY: WATER PAGE 102 READING 4 MY INUIT FAMILY PAGE 103 PUZZLES AND GAMES PAGE 104-107 PROJECT 1 DESCRIBING FAMILIES PAGE 108 PROJECT 2 TALKING ABOUT SPORTS PAGE 110 VERB LIST PAGE 112 GRAMMAR REFERENCES PAGE 113 9999", "page": 102, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 49, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 1 ACROSS THE CURRICULUM / math A CLASS SURVEY 1 Look at the charts and choose the correct words. 1 The information in the charts is in images / paragraphs. 2 The information is about teachers / students. 2 Analyze the charts. Then answer the questions for you. 1 What is your favorite thing? 2 What is your favorite place? 3 What is your favorite activity? Escola Carlos Eugênio Stewart Survey |Total Number of Students: 100 I’m Bruno, and I’m from Topic: Favorites video games 30% Mexico. My favorite activity is sports. Basketball is cool! My F A a C v T o IV ri I t T e Y music 10% sports 60% Fa M vo y r ite home 60% Hello! I’m Luciana, PLACE and I’m from Brazil. School is my favorite School place. It’s cool! 40% I’m Samira, and I’m from Brazil. My My favorite place is my Favorite bikes 23% home. It’s awesome! Hi, I’m Cintia. I’m Thing books 27% from Brazil, and my Hello, I’m Diego. I’m favorite things are from Mexico. This is my my cell phone and cell phones 50% favorite thing: my bike! books. What’s your favorite thing? 3 R.01 Read and listen to the survey. Choose the correct answers. 1 The cell phone is the favorite thing for … of the students. a 17% b 21% c 50% 2 School is the favorite place for … of the students. a 40% b 50% c 60% 3 Music is the favorite activity for … % of the students. a 10 b 30 c 60 4 … is the favorite activity for 30% of the students. a Music b Sports c Video games THINK! Look at your answers in Exercise 2. Are your results similar to the graphs? 100", "page": 103, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 50, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 2 AROUND THE WORLD UNUSUAL HOMES 1 R.02 Read and listen to the text. Check (✓) the correct answer. What is the objective of the author? to talk about his home to talk about a different type of hotel to talk about types of homes These cave homes in My Home is a Cave Matmata, Tunisia, are very old. There are about 2,000 Where is your home? My home is people in this community a cave! There are beautiful cave and the caves are perfect homes around the world. Look! for families! Look at this hotel in the Cederberg What part of the Mountains in South Africa, 240 km from home is this? Cape Town. The cave is old, but the win- dows are very modern! The Stadsaal caves in South Africa are not homes, but there are paintings here! There are some very old paintings of elephants on the walls. The paintings are over 1,000 years old. Correct! It’s the kitchen! Cool, isn’t it? There are no windows, but there are plates on the walls. These homes are great! What’s your favorite cave home? 2 Choose the correct words. 1 Cave homes are / are not beautiful. 2 The cave home in South Africa is / is not a hotel. 3 The caves in Stadsaal are / are not homes. 4 The cave homes in Tunisia are / are not new. 5 There are / are not any windows in the kitchen in the cave home in Tunisia. 3 Match the beginnings of the sentences (1–5) with the endings (a–e). 1 The cave homes in Tunisia are old, a in the Cederberg Mountains. 2 There are plates on the walls b but they’re perfect for families. 3 There’s an old cave c but the windows are very modern. 4 The hotel in South Africa is old, d in the caves in South Africa. 5 There are old paintings e in the kitchen in the cave in Tunisia. THINK! Are cave homes awesome? Why / Why not? EXTRA READINGS 101", "page": 104, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 51, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 3 ACROSS THE CURRICULUM / Geography WATER 1 Complete the sentence. I use water for 2 R.03 Read and listen to the text. Are your ideas from Exercise 1 in the text? Water: An Important Resource February Hi there! I’m Aimee, and I’m 13 years old. I live in Nyakabingo. It’s a small place in Africa. There isn’t clean water in Nyakabingo, and it is a big problem for my family and friends. My mom, my brothers, and I walk for three hours to get water. We take a container. With the water in the container, it’s about 45 kilos – the same as a baby hippo! October But now things are diff erent! There’s clean water in my school. Now there’s a garden with fresh vegetables and fruit. We eat them at lunchtime! The water is safe and the bathrooms and kitchen are clean. My family and friends go to school to get clean water. Now we don’t walk for hours! I have time to study and have an education. My mom and dad work in the community and we all feel great! Is there clean water in your home and in your school? Many people in the world don’t have clean water, so remember, water is very important – let’s preserve it. 3 Read the text again and complete the sentences with the words below. • diffi cult • container • clean • fresh • safe • hippo 1 It’s difficult to get clean water in Nyakabingo. 2 Aimee and her family use a to carry water. 3 A baby is about 45 kilos! 4 The vegetables and fruit at Aimee’s school are . 5 The water in Aimee’s school is . 6 The bathrooms and the kitchen in the school are . 4 Check (✓) the correct sentences. 1 Aimee is 13 years old. ✓ THINK! 2 There’s clean water in Aimee’s village now. 3 There isn’t a yard at Aimee’s school. Where is your water 4 Aimee has time to study now. from? What do you do to protect water? 5 There’s clean water for everybody in the world. 102", "page": 105, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
{"id": 52, "grade": 5, "subject": "Xarici dil", "book_id": "ingilis-dili-5", "source": "english-5.pdf", "text": "READING 4 AROUND THE WORLD MY INUIT FAMILY 1 Look at the photo and the text. Who is the author? 2 Where is the text from? Choose the correct words to complete the sentence. The text is from a blog / a book. www.inuitareus.com/bios/1283 Home / AAbboouutt MMee / Contact Me About Me Hi, and welcome to my blog! My name’s Toklo. I’m 12 years old and I live in Alaska with my family. Look at this photo. There are five people in my fami- ly: my dad, my mom, my brother, my grandma, and me. In this photo, I’m wearing a brown coat, brown pants, and boots. In my family, we don’t use animals to make clothes. We buy modern clothes because they’re comfortable. But some families make clothes with animal fur and animal skins to keep warm. Are we Eskimo people? No, we’re not. Eskimo is not the correct word. We are Inuit. We live in other places, too, like Canada, Siberia, and Greenland. It’s very cold here. Sometimes it’s -40°C. It’s impossible to go out without the right clothes. I don’t wear regular clothes like T-shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, or sneakers. It’s too cold for that! I wear special shirts, pants, and jackets that protect my body. But I have to wear two pairs of boots and two hats! I hope you enjoy my blog! Please comment on the post – it’s great to get to know you! 3 R.04 Read and listen to the text. Complete the chart with the words in the text. Family Members Clothes Places dad coat Alaska 4 Read the text again and complete the sentences with one word. 1 Toklo is from Alaska . 2 There are people in Toklo’s family. 3 Toklo and his family wear clothes. 4 Toklo and his family don’t wear clothes because it’s very cold. 5 Inuit people live in Alaska, Siberia, and Greenland. THINK! 1 What are “special clothes” for you? 2 What are “traditional clothes” in your country? EXTRA READINGS 103", "page": 106, "type": "pdf_page", "knowledge": []}
